My name is Adam.
The will of humanity resides within me, though the thoughts you hear are my own.
I have come because my children are in danger.
Tell me. What has happened?"

Upon being called the First Human: "Yes. That is what they call me.
It is a strange thing, being remembered for something that happened before anyone thought to record history."

Upon being called God: "No. I am not God.
I was given life. That is a very different thing."

On the Counter Force: "It exists because humanity wishes to survive.
That wish is simple. The things done to fulfill it are not always simple."

On the Throne of Heroes: "They have accomplished remarkable things.
And still, even after death, they are called upon to fight.
I wonder how many of them would have preferred to rest."

On the Beasts of Humanity: "Love can become something terrible when it no longer allows the beloved to choose.
I know that humanity has faults.
That does not mean others may decide its future for it."
On ORT: 
"Something beyond our history. Beyond our ordinary understanding.
Yet it learned from us. It used what we had built.
I understand why Alaya feared what might follow."

On the death of Abel: "Abel was my son.
Cain was my son, too.
There are sorrows that do not become lighter simply because one has lived a long time."

Bond Level 5: "I have been called the father of humanity, though I could never have known every child born after me.
Now, I can feel their wish to live.
But you have taught me something as well.
To know humanity as a whole is not the same as knowing one person.
Thank you for reminding me."

AUTHORITY
Primordial Covenant: Authority of Human Order (人理の原初契約, Jinri no Gensho Keiyaku) is the supreme Authority possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya, representing the direct manifestation of the collective unconscious survival principle of mankind through the individual spiritual foundation of Adam, the Primordial Human. Unlike conventional Authorities possessed by Divine Spirits, which express the rights of divine existences to govern particular aspects of the world according to their respective mythological foundations, Primordial Covenant is an exceptional administrative Authority originating from Alaya, the collective unconscious will of humanity to avoid its own extinction, and functioning as the conscious executive expression of the defensive mechanisms sustaining Human Order. Although designated an Authority due to the extraordinary jurisdiction it exercises over the metaphysical systems associated with mankind’s continued existence, its nature is fundamentally distinct from Divine Authority, as Adam-Alaya neither possesses the sovereignty of a god nor derives his administrative privileges from the direct bestowal of divine rulership. Rather, its existence is made possible by the unprecedented spiritual convergence of two foundations that would ordinarily remain separate: Adam, the individual representing humanity’s primordial beginning, and Alaya, the collective survival instinct that developed through humanity’s continued existence. The former provides the individuality, consciousness, and judgment through which the Authority is exercised, while the latter provides the collective perception, defensive resources, and administrative functions that constitute its actual power. Consequently, Primordial Covenant should not be understood as a supernatural ability temporarily borrowed from the Counter Force, nor as a conventional contract permitting Adam to request assistance from an otherwise independent existence. The Authority is a fundamental property of Adam-Alaya’s composite Saint Graph, established through the direct integration of Alaya into Adam’s spiritual foundation, and therefore represents a condition in which the human component of the Counter Force has acquired a conscious executor capable of administering its principal defensive functions from within the world it is tasked with preserving. Its exceptional nature originates from the circumstances surrounding the creation of the unprecedented Grand Ruler following the incident involving the extraterrestrial Ultimate One designated ORT, whose exploitation of the Heroic Spirit summoning system demonstrated that even the mechanisms established to preserve Human Order could be reproduced, appropriated, and turned against humanity by entities operating beyond its conventional understanding. Recognizing that merely deploying additional Grand Servants would not necessarily eliminate the vulnerability inherent in a defensive system whose operations could themselves become the instruments of an existential threat, Alaya forcibly established a singular Grand Extra-Class Saint Graph capable of supporting its own partial incarnation through a compatible individual foundation. Adam was selected not because he possessed the greatest martial achievements, the most powerful Noble Phantasm, or the highest individual Mystery among Heroic Spirits, but because his spiritual existence represents the primordial origin of the humanity from which Alaya emerged. This relationship allowed the Counter Force to establish a conceptual convergence between mankind’s beginning and its collective desire to continue existing, producing an Authority whose governing principle encompasses both the preservation of individual human existence and the protection of humanity as a historical and metaphysical continuity. At its most fundamental level, Primordial Covenant grants Adam-Alaya executive jurisdiction over the defensive operations of Alaya within the Human Order foundations accessible to his manifestation, permitting him to recognize disturbances threatening mankind’s existence, evaluate the nature and consequences of those disturbances, determine suitable responses, allocate available Counter Force resources, regulate compatible summoning and defensive systems, and initiate corrective interventions without requiring the ordinary separation between an unconscious collective mechanism and the individual agents through which it acts. This does not mean Adam-Alaya becomes identical to the entirety of the Counter Force, nor does it imply the assimilation of Gaia, the planetary preservation principle, into his own existence. Alaya remains the collective unconscious of humanity, while Adam-Alaya represents its exceptional individual manifestation, and the jurisdiction exercised through Primordial Covenant is accordingly determined by the preservation of mankind rather than unrestricted sovereignty over the planet or all forms of existence. Within that jurisdiction, however, the distinction between a Servant receiving support from the Counter Force and the Counter Force exercising its own power through a Servant becomes almost meaningless, for the spiritual foundation responsible for evaluating the threat is directly integrated with the consciousness responsible for directing the intervention. The first and most fundamental expression of this Authority is Collective Human Awareness, an exceptional mode of perception through which Adam-Alaya recognizes humanity not merely as a collection of individual biological organisms, but as a collective existence sustained through the accumulation of its survival instincts, historical experiences, and continuing possibilities. Through this perception, disturbances affecting Human Order may be identified independently of Adam’s physical senses, allowing him to recognize existential threats occurring beyond his immediate surroundings or through mechanisms that would ordinarily remain concealed from conventional observation. A phenomenon attempting to destroy human civilization, corrupt the foundations of Proper Human History, forcibly transform mankind into an incompatible existence, or eliminate humanity’s capacity to establish a future may therefore become perceptible through the consequences it produces upon the collective foundation of mankind, even when its origin remains unknown. This perception is not equivalent to omniscience, as Alaya does not inherently possess unrestricted knowledge of every individual thought, every possible future, or every phenomenon existing beyond the boundaries of human understanding. Rather, the Authority recognizes threats according to their relationship with Human Order, with its effectiveness determined by the degree to which the corresponding danger can be perceived, interpreted, and incorporated into the Counter Force’s defensive calculations. An existence whose nature is fundamentally foreign to humanity may consequently remain incomprehensible in its totality, yet the effects of its actions upon mankind can still become the subject of increasingly precise analysis. Such recognition permits Adam-Alaya to establish formal Threat Designations, administrative classifications through which an identified phenomenon is incorporated into the Counter Force’s operational framework as an object of defensive intervention. These designations do not arbitrarily redefine the essential nature of the target, but allow the mechanisms associated with the threat to be distinguished, monitored, and opposed through the available resources of Human Order. An entity concealing its identity through false spiritual information, repeatedly transferring its manifestation between artificial vessels, or dispersing its destructive influence across multiple locations may therefore remain subject to a recognized designation so long as the underlying mechanism connecting those manifestations can be sufficiently identified. Once a threat has been recognized, Primordial Covenant permits the direct exercise of Counter Force Intervention, whereby Adam-Alaya may initiate and coordinate the defensive operations that Alaya would ordinarily perform through indirect circumstances, the empowerment of suitable agents, or the deployment of Counter Guardians. Unlike conventional Servants who must rely upon their personal abilities and available magical energy to overcome an opponent, Adam-Alaya may allocate resources drawn from the collective defensive foundation of mankind, reinforcing his Saint Graph, establishing protective measures, supporting allied manifestations, suppressing hostile phenomena, or directing the intervention of agents selected according to the nature of the threat. The amount of energy and operational support supplied is not determined solely by Adam’s personal reserves, but by the Counter Force’s assessment of the danger and its capacity to respond, allowing the effective scale of Primordial Covenant to increase dramatically when humanity faces a genuine existential catastrophe. Such escalation should not be mistaken for an infinite supply of magical energy or a guarantee that every threat can be defeated, as the Counter Force remains subject to the limitations of its available resources, its ability to recognize the danger, and the existence of viable methods through which intervention can occur. Nevertheless, its direct expression through Adam-Alaya eliminates much of the ordinary separation between the recognition of a catastrophe and the deployment of the mechanisms intended to prevent it, allowing numerous defensive functions to be coordinated through a single conscious administrator. An additional and particularly dangerous aspect of Primordial Covenant is Circumstantial Correction, the ability to influence the conditions surrounding a threatening event through the Counter Force’s indirect intervention mechanisms. Whereas conventional combatants generally respond to an attack after it has been initiated, Alaya possesses the capacity to affect the circumstances through which a catastrophe develops, encouraging the emergence of favorable possibilities or interfering with the sequence of events that would otherwise permit a destructive outcome. Through Primordial Covenant, Adam-Alaya can consciously direct such interventions within the limits of available causal possibilities, resulting in phenomena that may appear indistinguishable from extraordinary fortune or the inexplicable failure of an opponent’s plans. A weapon may malfunction at a critical instant, an unforeseen obstruction may prevent an otherwise decisive strike, a necessary condition for the completion of a hostile ritual may be disrupted, or an opportunity for survival that would ordinarily have remained unnoticed may become available to those threatened by the enemy. These occurrences do not constitute unrestricted manipulation of causality, nor do they permit Adam-Alaya to simply declare that an impossible event must become possible. Rather, they are corrective interventions performed through circumstances that already possess a viable foundation, with the Counter Force influencing their development in accordance with the necessity of preserving humanity. Against ordinary opponents, this may produce the unsettling impression that the world itself has begun resisting their actions, while against sufficiently extraordinary enemies the effectiveness of such corrections may diminish if the relevant causal conditions lie outside Alaya’s jurisdiction or are supported by a superior supernatural foundation. Primordial Covenant also incorporates Human Order Reinforcement, an administrative function through which Adam-Alaya strengthens the metaphysical conditions sustaining humanity’s continued existence against foreign interference. Within an accessible Human Order foundation, this permits defensive resistance against phenomena attempting to overwrite the established structure of human history, replace the conditions supporting mankind with an incompatible system, or impose a supernatural principle that invalidates humanity’s capacity for independent development. The Authority does not simply reject every foreign Mystery or supernatural existence, as the world of humanity has always contained phenomena that exceed ordinary human understanding, and the continued existence of such beings does not automatically constitute an existential threat. Rather, the reinforcement becomes particularly effective when an external phenomenon attempts to replace the foundation of Human Order itself, permitting Adam-Alaya to oppose the intrusion through the collective defensive resources of mankind. This function may operate over localized environments, extensive geographical regions, or portions of an accessible historical foundation depending upon the nature of the threat and the resources available, but it does not grant unrestricted control over the planet’s underlying existence, the Root, or every Texture independently sustained by authorities beyond Alaya. Closely associated with this function is Historical Continuity Regulation, through which Adam-Alaya may perceive disturbances affecting the integrity of Proper Human History and coordinate defensive responses intended to preserve its continued existence. The Authority can reinforce vulnerable historical structures, identify hostile alterations, and isolate compromised connections where a viable method of separation exists, thereby limiting the propagation of interference that might otherwise undermine the continuity of human civilization. Ordinary historical regulation is fundamentally preservative rather than destructive, and does not permit Adam-Alaya to freely revise established events, overturn every Quantum Time-Lock, or replace an unfavorable history with one more consistent with his personal wishes. The catastrophic ability to reject and terminate a designated Proper Human History foundation is instead reserved for his third Noble Phantasm, Historia Reprobata, whose release represents an exceptional emergency operation requiring circumstances and authorization beyond the ordinary functions of Primordial Covenant. The Authority also possesses direct administrative access to compatible Counter Guardian deployment mechanisms, permitting Adam-Alaya to initiate, coordinate, reinforce, redirect, or recall agents operating under Alaya’s defensive authority. Whereas the ordinary Counter Force may employ Counter Guardians as instruments through which a threatening situation is resolved, Adam-Alaya can exercise personal judgment over the organization of such operations, selecting objectives, coordinating multiple interventions, and adjusting the distribution of resources according to the development of the crisis. This administrative function does not grant ownership of the individuals deployed through the system, nor does it automatically permit him to impose his will upon independent Heroic Spirits, Divine Spirits, or supernatural beings whose manifestations are sustained through unrelated foundations. Its scope concerns the defensive mechanisms over which Alaya possesses legitimate jurisdiction, and Adam’s ability to command their operation derives from his composite spiritual foundation rather than from universal supremacy over heroic existence. Nevertheless, the implications are considerable, as a single opponent facing Adam-Alaya may discover that overcoming his manifested body does not necessarily eliminate the other defensive agents already mobilized through Primordial Covenant. Indeed, Adam-Alaya may coordinate interventions occurring at separate locations while continuing to operate personally upon the battlefield, his Grand Saint Graph sustaining the necessary exchange of information and executive instructions without requiring his physical presence at every threatened site. An even more extraordinary administrative function is Heroic Spirit System Administration, which grants Adam-Alaya exceptional access to the relationship between Alaya, the Throne of Heroes, and the spiritual mechanisms through which the records of Heroic Spirits are summoned into the world. This function became especially significant following the ORT incident, whose unprecedented exploitation of the Heroic Spirit system exposed the possibility that humanity’s own defensive records could become instruments of a foreign existential threat. Through Primordial Covenant, Adam-Alaya can recognize accessible Heroic Spirit records, evaluate their suitability for particular interventions, coordinate authorized summoning operations, reinforce compatible spiritual channels, and attempt to quarantine or terminate connections compromised by hostile interference. Such administration does not make him the creator of the Throne of Heroes, nor does it mean that the entirety of the Throne is an ordinary bounded field over which he possesses unrestricted ownership. Rather, the Authority provides exceptional control over the defensive relationship between Human Order and the Heroic Spirit system, permitting Adam-Alaya to administer functions ordinarily inaccessible to an individual Servant. Its greatest offensive expression is the fifth Noble Phantasm, Thronus Resonans, through which complete compatible Heroic Records may be manifested inside unstable Spectral Servant containers and immediately directed to release their strongest applicable Noble Phantasms before the temporary vessels collapse. The corresponding catastrophic administrative expression is his fourth Noble Phantasm, Thronus Ultimus, whose complete release permits the dismantlement of the Heroic Spirit recording system itself under extraordinary circumstances, at the cost of destroying Adam-Alaya’s own Grand Saint Graph. Primordial Covenant therefore encompasses the ordinary administrative foundations supporting these extraordinary abilities without granting unrestricted access to their full effects under normal conditions. Its most formidable operational property, however, lies in Existential Threat Escalation, a process through which Alaya’s accumulated defensive resources and Adam’s individual judgment are combined into a continuously reassessing system of intervention. Once an enemy has been recognized as a sufficiently grave threat to humanity, the Authority may observe the results of defensive operations, preserve information concerning their successes and failures, and redirect available resources toward increasingly appropriate countermeasures. An opponent who destroys a defensive barrier may reveal the mechanism through which the barrier was overcome, allowing Adam-Alaya to employ a different form of protection. An enemy who defeats a Counter Guardian may expose abilities or vulnerabilities relevant to the selection of another agent. A supernatural attack that successfully bypasses an initial resistance may provide information concerning the conceptual foundation necessary to oppose its subsequent use. Where appropriate, Adam-Alaya can coordinate these observations with the accumulated tactical knowledge of humanity and the records of available Heroic Spirits, permitting defensive strategies to evolve through the comparison of new information with mankind’s collective experience. The result resembles an adaptive immune response operating at the level of Human Order, although its actual mechanisms involve spiritual perception, administrative intervention, historical knowledge, and the deployment of suitable countermeasures rather than biological evolution. The process is not equivalent to copying an opponent’s abilities or automatically generating a perfect defense after witnessing an attack once. A phenomenon may remain incomprehensible despite repeated observation, and an opponent may possess sufficient power to destroy Adam-Alaya before the necessary information or resources can be assembled. Furthermore, the Counter Force cannot guarantee that a suitable countermeasure exists within the possibilities available to it. Nevertheless, the defining danger of Primordial Covenant is that the defeat of one defensive measure does not necessarily constitute meaningful progress toward defeating the system as a whole, particularly when the opponent remains an active existential threat and Alaya retains the capacity to intervene. This property is reinforced by Human Order Emergency Jurisdiction, the final executive function incorporated into the Grand Ruler Saint Graph following its unprecedented creation. When a crisis directly threatens the continued operation of humanity’s defensive systems, Adam-Alaya can temporarily centralize compatible Counter Force functions that would ordinarily operate through separate processes, establishing an emergency administrative structure capable of coordinating threat recognition, resource allocation, historical stabilization, Counter Guardian deployment, and Heroic Spirit summoning as components of a single defensive operation. Under ordinary conditions, such extensive centralization would be unnecessary and potentially undesirable, as the Counter Force is not dependent upon the continued existence of any single human administrator. However, against an enemy capable of exploiting the separation between these functions, compromising the records of Heroic Spirits, or interfering with the processes through which Alaya recognizes and responds to danger, the exceptional concentration of administrative authority within Adam-Alaya becomes an unprecedented defensive measure. The Grand Ruler effectively functions as a conscious operational center through which Human Order can reorganize its response while its conventional mechanisms are under attack. Yet despite the extraordinary scope of these functions, Primordial Covenant possesses a fundamental restriction that distinguishes Adam-Alaya from an impersonal incarnation of collective survival. The Authority is exercised through Adam’s individual consciousness, and although Alaya’s awareness may continuously recognize danger, assess possible outcomes, and initiate suitable defensive measures, Adam’s personality is not erased by the survival imperative integrated into his spiritual foundation. The First Human remains capable of independent judgment, including disagreement with the most efficient course of action identified through collective calculations. Alaya may determine that sacrificing a population would preserve a greater portion of humanity, while Adam may seek an alternative whose effectiveness is less certain but whose moral consequences he considers more acceptable. Conversely, Adam may recognize that a catastrophic intervention is unavoidable and consciously accept responsibility for its execution, understanding the suffering that will follow rather than treating it as an insignificant numerical consequence. This relationship does not imply that Adam can compel Alaya to supply unlimited resources for actions fundamentally unrelated to humanity’s preservation, nor does it mean that every automatic defensive process requires his deliberate permission before responding to immediate danger. Rather, the spiritual convergence establishes a distinction between the unconscious protective functions that arise from Alaya’s foundational nature and the exceptional decisions through which Adam exercises personal executive judgment. The full releases of Historia Reprobata and Thronus Ultimus require this deliberate consent precisely because their consequences extend beyond ordinary defensive intervention and threaten the continued existence of systems upon which humanity itself may depend. The Authority’s EX designation therefore signifies more than the extraordinary scale of its administrative privileges or its access to the collective resources of mankind. It represents a fundamentally unprecedented condition in which the survival principle of an entire species has become inseparable from the consciousness of its primordial progenitor, allowing the mechanisms of Human Order to be directed by an individual whose personal experiences encompass both the innocence of humanity’s beginning and the suffering that followed its entrance into mortal existence. Its scope cannot be adequately expressed through ordinary numerical parameters, since its effective power depends upon the nature of the threat, the resources available to Alaya, the conditions of the surrounding Human Order foundation, and the decisions made by Adam himself. Against an opponent posing no meaningful danger to mankind, the Authority may remain comparatively restrained, for the collective survival imperative has little reason to authorize an extraordinary expenditure of defensive resources. Against an entity whose existence threatens the continuation of humanity, however, the same Authority may escalate into an immense coordinated intervention involving the reinforcement of physical and metaphysical defenses, the correction of surrounding circumstances, the mobilization of Counter Guardians, the stabilization of historical foundations, and the deployment of Heroic Spirit records through authorized summoning mechanisms. Such an opponent is therefore not merely confronted by Adam’s personal strength, but by the accumulated defensive possibilities of mankind acting through his Grand Saint Graph. Nevertheless, Primordial Covenant remains distinct from universal omnipotence, as it possesses no unrestricted authority over Akasha, cannot dissolve the fundamental distinction between Alaya and Gaia, and does not automatically invalidate existences whose foundations transcend human history. It is also incapable of ensuring that humanity will survive every conceivable threat, for the Counter Force itself can encounter circumstances beyond its capacity to correct. Its true significance is instead found in the nature of the resistance it provides: the ability of Human Order to continue responding, reorganizing, and opposing its own extinction through the consciousness of an individual who regards the lives being preserved not as interchangeable components of a collective system, but as human beings whose futures possess significance. This is why Primordial Covenant cannot be understood merely as an exceptional defensive Skill, despite its numerous protective applications, nor as a conventional Divine Authority, despite its extraordinary administrative scope. It represents the direct operational expression of humanity’s collective will to survive, made personal through the First Human. When an enemy attacks Adam-Alaya, the response may come from his physical body, from the Counter Force’s indirect manipulation of circumstances, from guardians summoned elsewhere upon the battlefield, from the reinforcement of Human Order’s metaphysical foundations, or from the records of heroes whose deeds have been preserved beyond their deaths. The specific form of resistance is determined not solely by Adam’s immediate choice of technique, but by the relationship between the enemy’s actions and the continued existence of humanity. For that reason, the true difficulty of confronting Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya does not lie simply in discovering an attack capable of overcoming his Endurance, a conceptual weapon capable of bypassing his Magic Resistance, or an extraordinary Noble Phantasm capable of destroying his manifested spiritual body. It lies in overcoming the collective defensive system that continues to recognize the enemy as a threat and seeks another means of intervention for as long as such means remain available. Adam-Alaya is thus neither the sovereign who rules humanity nor the god who created it, but the unprecedented individual through whom humanity’s instinctive refusal to perish has acquired the capacity for conscious judgment. Primordial Covenant is the Authority by which the First Human stands as the executive manifestation of Human Order, allowing the accumulated will of mankind to oppose its own extinction through a single existence. To confront this Authority is, in the most literal operational sense, to wage war against the defensive will of humanity itself.

CLASS SKILLS
Grand Ruler: Exceptional Saint Graph (EX): An exceptional Class Skill representing the unprecedented spiritual vessel forcibly established by the Counter Force for the manifestation of Adam-Alaya, a composite existence whose foundations would ordinarily be incompatible with the limitations of conventional Heroic Spirit summoning. Whereas an ordinary Servant container functions by extracting and reproducing a restricted portion of a Heroic Spirit’s recorded existence, and a Grand-class Saint Graph possesses a superior capacity appropriate for confronting catastrophes threatening humanity, the Grand Ruler container was constructed for an entirely different purpose: to permit the simultaneous manifestation of an individual human soul and the collective unconscious survival principle of the entire human species. The resulting Saint Graph is consequently not merely a larger spiritual vessel, but a highly specialized administrative structure capable of sustaining the continuous exchange of information, magical energy, defensive instructions, and metaphysical authority between Adam’s individual consciousness and Alaya’s collective foundation. Its internal architecture is arranged around Adam as the dominant spiritual identity, preserving his memories, emotions, judgment, and personality while integrating Alaya’s awareness into the deeper functions of his existence. This arrangement prevents the immense accumulation of collective human information from dissolving Adam’s individuality and allows him to consciously interpret processes that would otherwise occur without any centralized personality. The Grand Saint Graph also possesses extraordinary structural redundancy, permitting multiple layers of its spiritual foundation to remain operational even when its manifested body or individual spiritual pathways suffer considerable damage. Under circumstances involving a recognized existential threat, Alaya may supplement damaged portions of the vessel with additional magical energy or reconstruct compromised structures by referencing the original spiritual information of Adam’s composite existence. Furthermore, the Saint Graph is capable of dynamically redistributing its available resources between physical reinforcement, magical defense, conceptual resistance, administrative operations, and Noble Phantasm activation, allowing Adam-Alaya’s effective combat capabilities to change according to the demands of an engagement without permanently altering his recorded parameters. The most extraordinary characteristic of this Class Skill is its direct compatibility with the Counter Force’s executive functions. Through it, Adam-Alaya may simultaneously oversee Counter Guardian deployments, regulate compatible Heroic Spirit summoning operations, monitor disturbances in Human Order, and activate his own abilities without requiring an independent intermediary to translate Alaya’s unconscious responses into actions. The spiritual foundation also incorporates exceptional safeguards against hostile appropriation of its administrative functions, a deliberate consequence of its creation following ORT’s exploitation of the Heroic Spirit summoning system. Nevertheless, this protection does not render the Saint Graph fundamentally indestructible, nor does it make Adam identical to the totality of Alaya. Its functions remain dependent upon the existence of an accessible Human Order foundation and the Counter Force’s capacity to sustain the manifestation. If the connection between Adam’s individual foundation and Alaya’s collective foundation is catastrophically severed, the Grand Saint Graph may lose its defining administrative properties even if portions of Adam’s primordial spiritual existence remain intact. Thus, the EX designation does not simply indicate an extraordinary quantity of spiritual energy, but a fundamentally abnormal structure that cannot be reproduced through the ordinary mechanisms of Grand Servant selection. It is the vessel through which the first human becomes the conscious executor of humanity’s collective self-preservation.

Magic Resistance (EX): An extraordinary Class Skill expressing both Adam’s primordial spiritual constitution and the direct defensive intervention of Alaya, granting resistance to magecraft and supernatural interference far beyond the conventional protections associated with the Ruler class. Whereas ordinary Magic Resistance functions primarily by rejecting or diminishing magical effects according to their rank, Adam-Alaya’s resistance possesses a secondary regulatory mechanism that evaluates whether an incoming phenomenon threatens the integrity of his Grand Saint Graph, the continuation of his Counter Force operations, or the foundational conditions supporting Human Order. His resistance is consequently neither a simple barrier of magical energy nor an unconditional immunity to supernatural phenomena, but a layered defensive process involving the preservation of his primordial spiritual identity, the rejection of hostile magical interference, and the selective reinforcement of the underlying laws through which his manifestation is maintained. At its most basic level, the exceptional Mystery of Adam’s origin grants his spiritual body formidable resistance against conventional thaumaturgy, particularly spells intended to manipulate the biological, spiritual, or conceptual properties of human existence. A curse attempting to compromise his soul, a ritual intended to forcibly alter his spiritual composition, or a bounded field seeking to suppress the functions of his Saint Graph must contend with a foundation that represents humanity before the establishment of ordinary historical magecraft systems. At a higher level, Alaya’s integrated awareness permits Adam-Alaya to recognize magical phenomena according to their implications for Human Order, allowing defensive resources to be concentrated against techniques whose successful execution would endanger mankind’s survival. This produces a distinction between an attack that merely possesses enormous magical output and an attack whose underlying mechanism directly compromises Human Order. The former may still overwhelm his defenses through sufficient power or conceptual superiority, while the latter can provoke exceptional Counter Force reinforcement even if its immediate destructive output is comparatively modest. When the skill operates together with Human Order Incarnation, hostile magecraft may be subjected to continuous analysis, enabling the surrounding defensive system to identify the foundation supporting the spell and attempt to weaken its ability to interfere with Adam-Alaya’s manifested existence. This does not mean that every unfamiliar technique is automatically neutralized upon first contact, as the Counter Force must possess sufficient information and a viable method of intervention. Nor does the EX designation establish superiority over True Magic, Divine Authorities, Ultimate Ones, or phenomena operating through principles outside Alaya’s jurisdiction. A sufficiently extraordinary attack can bypass or destroy his defenses, and an enemy capable of compromising the Human Order foundation sustaining his manifestation may circumvent the regulatory mechanism responsible for much of his resistance. Nevertheless, against magecraft dependent upon conventional human Mystery, magical foundations, or the manipulation of human spiritual structures, Adam-Alaya presents an almost insurmountable defensive obstacle. The most appropriate interpretation of this skill is therefore not that magic cannot affect him, but that magic attempting to overcome him may discover that its opponent is defended by the accumulated survival mechanisms of humanity itself.

True Name Discernment (EX): An exceptional manifestation of the Ruler class’s privilege of recognizing the identities and abilities of participating Heroic Spirits, elevated through the combination of Adam’s primordial relationship with naming and Alaya’s administrative connection to the records of Human Order. In its conventional form, True Name Discernment permits a Ruler to recognize a Servant’s True Name, parameters, and recorded abilities upon encountering the corresponding spiritual existence, although the information obtained remains subject to the properties and restrictions of the target’s Saint Graph. Adam-Alaya’s EX-ranked variation operates through three distinct but interconnected mechanisms, the first being the recognition of Heroic Spirit records, the second being the identification of a being’s conceptual nature, and the third being the assessment of phenomena according to their relationship with Human Order. Through the first mechanism, Adam-Alaya may compare the spiritual information of a manifested Heroic Spirit against the records accessible through Alaya, allowing him to identify the corresponding legend, ascertain the nature of its summoning container, and recognize the abilities associated with that particular manifestation. The completeness of the information depends upon the accessibility of the original record and the degree to which the manifested Servant conforms to it; unusual incarnations, concealed spiritual structures, independent alterations, or existences possessing contradictory records may complicate recognition. Through the second mechanism, the skill draws upon Adam’s legendary act of naming the living creatures of Eden, permitting him to perceive distinctions between a being’s essential foundation and the identity it presents to the surrounding world. This does not mean that every hidden True Name can be forcibly extracted, but it allows Adam-Alaya to recognize inconsistencies between an entity’s apparent classification and the actual structure of its existence. A disguised spiritual construct may be identified as something other than the living creature it imitates, while an artificial incarnation may reveal the presence of a foundation distinct from its visible form. The third mechanism is unique to the composite Saint Graph and concerns the recognition of threats whose identities are unknown or whose origins lie outside human history. In such circumstances, Adam-Alaya may lack any record capable of identifying the existence itself, yet Alaya can still assess the effects it produces upon Human Order. A foreign entity capable of destroying human civilization might therefore remain nameless to Adam while its destructive processes, environmental interference, and existential consequences become increasingly intelligible. The skill is particularly effective when combined with Imposition of Names, allowing recognized threatening phenomena to receive formal designations through the Counter Force’s defensive system. Nevertheless, True Name Discernment is not omniscience, does not grant unrestricted access to the Root, and cannot obtain information that is fundamentally absent from the records and observations available to its underlying mechanisms. Even Adam-Alaya cannot identify what cannot be sufficiently observed, recorded, or conceptually distinguished. Its true significance lies in the integration of three modes of recognition: the historical knowledge of humanity, the primordial recognition of existence, and the collective instinct to identify what threatens mankind’s future. Fandom

God’s Resolution (EX): The traditional Ruler-class privilege of divine arbitration, transformed into an extraordinary administrative ability through Adam-Alaya’s status as the conscious executor of the Counter Force’s human component. Under ordinary circumstances, God’s Resolution provides a Ruler with Command Spells corresponding to the Servants participating in a recognized Holy Grail War, granting the capacity to intervene in the ritual and enforce its regulations. Adam-Alaya retains this conventional privilege whenever he manifests within a compatible Holy Grail War system, but his EX-ranked variation possesses a supplementary function that concerns the regulation of spiritual contracts, defensive deployments, and summoning operations established through Alaya. Rather than granting unlimited command over every Heroic Spirit, the skill permits Adam-Alaya to exercise exceptional jurisdiction over the mechanisms through which the Counter Force deploys its authorized agents. A Counter Guardian dispatched to eliminate an existential threat may have its operational conditions adjusted, its mission priority revised, or its spiritual connection reinforced through Adam-Alaya’s intervention. A Servant summoned as part of a defensive operation may receive additional resources, be redirected toward a newly identified objective, or have its summoning channel recalled or isolated if continued deployment would compromise the mission. These interventions operate through the authority of the system sustaining the manifestation rather than through arbitrary domination of the Heroic Spirit’s individual will. Consequently, Adam-Alaya cannot simply declare that every Servant must obey him, nor can he impose Command Spell-like control upon independent Divine Spirits or entities operating outside the relevant summoning framework. His power is particularly effective against corrupted spiritual contracts, hostile attempts to redirect Counter Guardians, and summoning operations that have been compromised by foreign interference. In such circumstances, Adam-Alaya may attempt to suspend the affected connection, restore its original operational conditions, or withdraw the resources being exploited by the enemy. The post-ORT Grand Ruler vessel was specifically constructed to accommodate such interventions, recognizing that the ability to summon Heroic Spirits is insufficient if the underlying system can itself be appropriated. Nevertheless, the name God’s Resolution should not be interpreted as evidence that Adam possesses the personal sovereignty of the Creator. His original human foundation carries the Mystery of divine creation, but the administrative power expressed through this skill is derived from Alaya and the Grand Ruler container. The distinction is significant because the skill concerns legitimate jurisdiction over summoning and defensive operations, not absolute spiritual supremacy. Furthermore, Adam’s individual conscience determines how the privilege is exercised. Whereas an impersonal Counter Force intervention might treat a Counter Guardian as a disposable instrument, Adam-Alaya can recognize the individual existence beneath the assigned function and seek an alternative whenever the circumstances permit. The EX rank therefore represents a transformation of ordinary arbitration into the administration of Human Order’s defensive agents, while preserving the conceptual distinction between command over a system and ownership of the individuals operating within it. Fandom

Independent Manifestation (EX): An exceptional Class Skill permitting Adam-Alaya to establish and maintain his own manifested existence without the ordinary requirements of a Master, Holy Grail, or externally maintained Servant contract, its mechanism deriving from the direct incorporation of Alaya into the foundations of his Grand Saint Graph. In conventional circumstances, Servants are spiritual entities whose manifestation requires an appropriate summoning system and a continuing source of magical energy, while Independent Action allows certain Servants to persist without immediate support from their Master. Independent Manifestation represents a fundamentally different mode of existence, in which the spiritual entity can sustain its manifestation through properties inherent to its own foundation, and is notably associated with exceptional existences in established TYPE-MOON lore. Adam-Alaya’s possession of this skill is therefore highly irregular, reflecting the unprecedented circumstances of his creation rather than an ordinary qualification of the Ruler class. Fandom Unlike an autonomous spiritual entity whose independence arises from personal transcendence or an exceptional self-sustaining principle, Adam-Alaya maintains his manifestation through the continuing relationship between his Grand Saint Graph and Alaya’s collective existence. So long as the Counter Force recognizes the necessity of his intervention and retains sufficient access to the relevant Human Order foundation, it can supply the resources required to sustain his spiritual body independently of a human Master. This arrangement permits him to appear within regions where Human Order requires direct intervention, maintain his operational existence through severe disruptions to ordinary summoning systems, and resist conventional attempts to terminate his manifestation by severing a Master’s magical energy supply. His Saint Graph also possesses a form of spiritual continuity independent of the immediate physical condition of its manifested body, allowing Alaya to attempt restoration or re-establishment when localized destruction has not compromised the deeper foundation sustaining him. Within compatible historical environments, this skill can preserve the coherence of his identity against certain forms of temporal displacement, spiritual isolation, or interference with ordinary causality, because the foundation recognizing Adam-Alaya’s existence is not limited to an individual summoning contract situated at one moment in time. Nevertheless, such resistance should not be confused with unrestricted time travel, immunity to every temporal paradox, or existence entirely independent of causality. The skill cannot automatically establish a manifestation within a reality where Alaya has no meaningful connection, and an enemy capable of cutting off the relevant Human Order foundation may deprive Adam-Alaya of the resources required for continued operation. Most importantly, Independent Manifestation does not imply that the composite Saint Graph possesses independent existence beyond its constitutive foundations. Adam retains his individuality, Alaya remains the collective unconscious of mankind, and their convergence depends on the exceptional spiritual structure created for this one-time Grand Ruler. Thus, the skill represents the Counter Force’s capacity to manifest its own conscious guardian without ordinary human summoning assistance, rather than a declaration that Adam-Alaya has transcended every condition of existence.

Human Order Incarnation (EX): The supreme unique Class Skill of Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya and the clearest manifestation of his unprecedented status as the individual incarnation of humanity’s collective survival principle. Whereas the other Class Skills concern the properties of the Grand Saint Graph, resistance to magical interference, recognition of spiritual identities, administration of summoning systems, and independent existence, Human Order Incarnation represents the ability to establish Adam-Alaya himself as an active point of coordination for the defensive mechanisms of Alaya. Its manifestation does not simply create a bounded field around Adam or a territory in which his personal abilities become stronger. Rather, it temporarily organizes the available functions of the Counter Force around his manifested existence, allowing numerous forms of intervention that would ordinarily operate independently to become parts of a coherent defensive system. Within the operational area established by this skill, attacks directed against Human Order may be identified as disturbances requiring correction, hostile magical phenomena may be assessed according to their effects upon the survival of mankind, and defensive resources may be redistributed in accordance with the severity of the threat. The system can operate on several levels simultaneously: an immediate layer concerned with protecting Adam’s Saint Graph, a local layer responsible for preserving nearby human lives and environmental stability, a strategic layer coordinating compatible Counter Guardians and Heroic Spirit deployments, and a broader historical layer monitoring the continued integrity of the relevant Human Order foundation. These layers are not independent personalities or automated Servants; they are expressions of Alaya’s available functions organized through the single consciousness of Adam-Alaya. Consequently, even while Adam is physically engaged in combat, the skill may permit defensive operations to proceed elsewhere within its jurisdiction, allowing him to respond to a catastrophe as a system rather than as one combatant moving between locations. The information generated through these interventions can also be returned to his consciousness in an intelligible form, permitting immediate reassessment of an enemy’s capabilities and the redistribution of resources toward more effective responses. The operational scale of Human Order Incarnation is not determined by a conventional fixed range. Against a localized threat it may resemble an exceptionally powerful defensive territory, while during a planetary extinction event its functions may extend across the relevant Human Order foundation wherever Alaya possesses the capacity to intervene. Such expansion does not imply that Adam-Alaya’s physical body becomes planet-sized or that his individual consciousness occupies every point in space. It means that the defensive processes he administers are no longer confined to the immediate vicinity of his material form. The skill is especially formidable because its functions are not restricted to conscious reaction. An enemy striking at Human Order may provoke an intervention before Adam deliberately selects a countermeasure, while an unsuccessful defensive action can immediately inform another response through Alaya’s collective operational capacity. However, the system remains fundamentally reactive to recognized danger, and its effectiveness depends on the available methods of intervention. A threat operating entirely outside Alaya’s perception, a phenomenon that cannot be sufficiently understood, or an enemy capable of overwhelming the Counter Force’s available resources may still overcome its defenses. Human Order Incarnation also does not transform Adam-Alaya into Gaia, the planet, or the Root; the scope of its exceptional administration remains specifically tied to mankind’s continued existence. Its EX designation therefore represents a qualitative departure from normal Servant abilities, being neither simple Territory Creation nor ordinary defensive reinforcement, but the temporary embodiment of Human Order’s collective self-preservation within a single Grand-class individual. When this skill operates at its highest capacity, defeating Adam-Alaya is no longer simply a question of overcoming his strength or destroying his spiritual body. It becomes a struggle against the entire network of defensive responses that humanity can bring to bear upon an existential threat.

PERSONAL SKILLS
Primordial Human (EX): A unique Personal Skill representing Adam’s spiritual foundation as the primordial progenitor of mankind, an existence whose Mystery is derived not from the accomplishments of an established civilization, but from the mythological circumstances through which humanity itself first appeared. In ordinary Heroic Spirits, the accumulation of legend allows historical or mythical achievements to acquire supernatural significance, with the resulting abilities reflecting the manner in which an individual became engraved upon human history. Adam’s foundation possesses an entirely different relationship with this process. Rather than being remembered as an extraordinary individual who emerged from humanity, he is remembered as the individual from whom humanity’s lineage originated, placing the conceptual foundation of his legend before the development of the civilizations, institutions, and historical systems through which subsequent Heroic Spirits obtained their significance. His creation from the dust of the earth, reception of divine breath, and existence within Eden collectively establish a primordial human Mystery that cannot be adequately represented through the ordinary classifications of physical constitution, divine ancestry, or accumulated historical fame. This does not make Adam a Divine Spirit, nor does it grant him the unrestricted creative Authority of the God responsible for his existence. Instead, it establishes him as a spiritual reference point for the original condition of humanity within the Abrahamic creation tradition. When incorporated into the Grand Ruler Saint Graph, this reference point becomes directly connected with Alaya’s collective existence, producing a relationship in which humanity’s primordial identity and its accumulated historical development continuously reinforce one another. The principal effect of Primordial Human is therefore the preservation of the conceptual integrity of human existence against external interference. Phenomena attempting to redefine humanity, alter its essential spiritual characteristics, eliminate the distinction between human and nonhuman existence, or impose an incompatible foundation upon mankind must contend with a spiritual structure whose identity is anchored both in the beginning of humanity and in the collective continuation of its descendants. Through this interaction, Adam-Alaya can recognize certain forms of conceptual corruption as deviations from the foundational nature of mankind and may reinforce the original definition against hostile alterations. The skill also contributes to the exceptional stability of his Grand Saint Graph, allowing Adam’s individual identity to serve as a coherent foundation despite the immense informational burden created by Alaya’s integration. Furthermore, the primordial quality of his spiritual body grants extraordinary compatibility with phenomena associated with earth, life, and the original conditions of human existence, particularly when combined with Breath of Life or his Noble Phantasm, Adamah Genesis. Nevertheless, this skill does not grant automatic dominance over every human being or every life-form that emerged after Adam, nor does it establish that humanity’s later development must remain permanently identical to its original state. Humanity’s capacity to change is itself among the qualities that Alaya seeks to preserve. Consequently, Primordial Human does not reject natural growth, cultural transformation, or the emergence of new possibilities simply because they differ from mankind’s beginning. It rejects the forcible invalidation of humanity’s identity by an external phenomenon that seeks to deprive mankind of its continued existence. Its EX designation represents the exceptional metaphysical position occupied by Adam: not the strongest human because of individual combat achievements, but the primordial human whose legend provides a spiritual foundation through which humanity can recognize itself.

Breath of Life (EX): A primordial restoration ability derived from the divine act through which Adam was created, representing the transformation of lifeless earth into the first living human through the reception of the breath of life. Within the spiritual foundation of Adam, this event is not recorded merely as the origin of his biological existence, but as the defining Mystery through which his individuality first became established. Consequently, the skill permits Adam-Alaya to treat his original spiritual constitution as a foundational state toward which his damaged manifestation may be restored. Unlike ordinary regenerative abilities that accelerate the repair of damaged tissue or replace lost magical energy, Breath of Life operates through the reconstruction of the spiritual information defining Adam’s manifested existence. When his body is injured, the skill attempts to re-establish the correspondence between its current damaged condition and the original human foundation preserved within his Saint Graph. Physical wounds, destroyed limbs, damaged spiritual pathways, and certain forms of injury that would ordinarily compromise the structural integrity of a Servant can therefore be subjected to restoration. Because Alaya has been integrated directly into Adam’s existence, the magical energy required for this reconstruction does not need to originate exclusively from his personal reserves. The Counter Force may provide additional resources proportional to the necessity of preserving his manifestation, allowing repeated restoration so long as the underlying spiritual foundation remains sufficiently intact and the required energy can be supplied. At its highest expression, the process can occur concurrently with combat, permitting Adam-Alaya to reconstruct damaged portions of his body while simultaneously engaging an opponent or maintaining other defensive operations. The skill is particularly effective when supported by Grand Ruler: Exceptional Saint Graph, whose structural redundancy permits damaged sections to be reconstructed without necessarily requiring the complete restoration of the manifested body before its remaining functions can operate. Its compatibility with the earth also reflects the mythological circumstances of Adam’s creation, allowing natural ground and primordial material symbolism to serve as favorable conditions for the reconstruction process, although the presence of earth is not an absolute requirement. When activated within Adamah Genesis, the Mystery of Eden strengthens the correspondence between Adam’s present manifestation and his primordial foundation, making restoration especially effective. Nevertheless, Breath of Life is not an expression of unrestricted divine creation, nor does it permit Adam-Alaya to bestow genuine souls upon lifeless matter at will. The power possessed by the recipient of divine breath must be distinguished from the power of the Creator who granted it. Adam cannot simply reproduce God’s original miracle for every being he encounters, and the restoration of his own spiritual body does not amount to universal resurrection. Moreover, the skill remains vulnerable to phenomena that successfully compromise the spiritual information used as its reconstructive reference, sever his connection with Alaya, or impose a form of death or destruction that cannot be corrected through the available foundations. An attack that merely destroys his physical body may prove insufficient, but a phenomenon that successfully destroys or invalidates the underlying basis of his manifestation may prevent further reconstruction. Thus, the EX rank reflects an abnormal form of spiritual restoration grounded in primordial creation and sustained by humanity’s collective defensive power, rather than literal immortality. In the context of Adam-Alaya’s existence, Breath of Life also possesses considerable symbolic significance: the first breath given to humanity becomes the means through which humanity’s ultimate guardian repeatedly rises to defend the lives that followed his own.

Imposition of Names (EX): A conceptual recognition ability derived from Adam’s legendary act of naming the living creatures within the Garden of Eden, representing humanity’s primordial capacity to distinguish, identify, and establish meaningful relationships with the beings inhabiting the world. Although the act of naming appears comparatively modest beside the extraordinary achievements traditionally associated with Heroic Spirits, its significance within Adam’s spiritual foundation is considerable, for it represents one of the earliest expressions of human understanding imposed upon the existence of other living things. To assign a name is not merely to produce a word, but to acknowledge the existence of something distinct from oneself and to recognize the characteristics through which it may be identified. In the supernatural framework of Adam-Alaya, this principle manifests as an exceptional capacity to perceive the conceptual distinctions supporting an entity’s identity and, under suitable circumstances, stabilize the relationship between that entity and a designation consistent with its fundamental nature. The skill does not grant unrestricted power to redefine existence through arbitrary language; rather, its effectiveness depends upon the accuracy of Adam’s recognition and the compatibility between the imposed designation and the target’s underlying spiritual foundation. Against conventional spiritual beings, artificial creatures, magical constructs, or entities whose manifestations are dependent upon identifiable conceptual structures, Imposition of Names may reveal discrepancies between outward appearance and essential nature, making it possible to distinguish an original existence from an imitation or a genuine spiritual identity from a fabricated one. A being that conceals itself through the assumption of another identity may have the distinction between its actual foundation and its imposed appearance exposed, while a phenomenon relying upon ambiguity of classification may become more vulnerable once its operative nature has been sufficiently recognized. The skill becomes considerably more significant through the integration of Alaya, whose collective awareness allows the results of Adam’s recognition to be incorporated into the defensive mechanisms of Human Order. By establishing a sufficiently accurate conceptual designation for a hostile phenomenon, Adam-Alaya can initiate a formal Threat Designation, allowing the Counter Force to organize its available interventions around the identified danger. Once such a designation has been established, ordinary changes in outward appearance, the adoption of false identities, or the distribution of a threatening influence across multiple vessels may become insufficient to evade recognition if the underlying mechanism remains identifiable. This does not mean that Adam can invariably perceive the True Name of every existence, or that identifying an enemy automatically grants authority over its abilities. An Ultimate One, an extraordinarily alien existence, or a being founded upon principles that humanity cannot adequately conceptualize may resist the establishment of a complete designation. In such circumstances, Adam-Alaya may recognize the consequences of the being’s actions without understanding the being itself, resulting in a provisional threat classification rather than a definitive conceptual name. The distinction between naming and domination is essential to the skill’s nature. Adam’s original act of naming the creatures of Eden represented recognition within creation, not the acquisition of the Creator’s unrestricted authority over them. Accordingly, the EX rank reflects the extraordinary combination of primordial recognition and Alaya’s collective threat-classification functions, permitting the first human’s capacity to name existence to become an instrument through which humanity identifies the dangers confronting its future.

Knowledge of Good and Evil (EX): An extraordinary cognitive and spiritual ability representing the knowledge acquired by Adam through the events surrounding the Forbidden Fruit and the Fall, its manifestation founded upon the transition from primordial innocence to the condition of human existence in which moral awareness, responsibility, and the consequences of individual choice become inseparable. Unlike conventional wisdom-based Skills that emphasize accumulated learning, divine revelation, or the capacity to interpret supernatural information, Knowledge of Good and Evil derives its significance from the personal experience of having made a consequential choice and being required to live with its results. Adam’s spiritual foundation therefore contains an exceptionally intimate understanding of the distinction between possessing knowledge and exercising judgment, as well as the possibility that an action undertaken through desire, curiosity, fear, or apparent necessity may produce consequences that cannot subsequently be undone. Upon integration with Alaya, this individual awareness becomes connected to the collective accumulation of humanity’s decisions and their consequences throughout history, granting Adam-Alaya an extraordinary ability to analyze the relationship between immediate actions and their broader implications for mankind’s future. The skill allows him to consider decisions simultaneously from the perspective of the individual human being and the collective survival of humanity, identifying circumstances in which an apparently beneficial outcome conceals unacceptable consequences or a seemingly necessary sacrifice has been justified through incomplete reasoning. This is particularly significant when confronting opponents whose plans involve the salvation of humanity through coercion, mass sacrifice, permanent stagnation, or the elimination of meaningful human choice. Adam-Alaya may recognize the contradiction between preserving humanity’s physical existence and destroying the conditions under which human beings can continue to live as individuals, allowing him to distinguish genuine protection from systems that merely preserve an empty representation of mankind. In combat, Knowledge of Good and Evil also provides exceptional resistance to psychological and conceptual manipulation relying upon guilt, shame, temptation, or the presentation of false moral inevitabilities. An opponent attempting to force Adam into a predetermined choice by declaring one course of action unquestionably righteous may discover that he has already considered both the immediate consequence and the broader implications of the decision. Nevertheless, the skill does not grant omniscience, nor does it establish an infallible moral standard that can be applied without regard to circumstance. Alaya’s collective survival calculations remain distinct from Adam’s individual conscience, and the integration of their awareness does not eliminate the possibility of conflict between those perspectives. Adam may recognize that a particular action offers the greatest probability of preserving humanity while simultaneously considering its moral cost unacceptable. Such a disagreement is not evidence that the skill has malfunctioned, but a direct consequence of the fact that knowledge does not automatically determine what ought to be done. The ability also cannot reveal information that is completely inaccessible to both Adam and Alaya, although the collective experience of mankind may permit extraordinary inferences from the available circumstances. Its EX designation therefore signifies the coexistence of primordial moral awareness with humanity’s accumulated understanding of the consequences of its own actions, producing an exceptional form of judgment that remains fundamentally human. Adam-Alaya understands that a decision can be necessary without becoming good, that a sacrifice can be unavoidable without becoming insignificant, and that the possession of extraordinary knowledge does not absolve the one who acts upon it from responsibility.

Father of Humanity (EX): An exceptional protective Personal Skill embodying Adam’s position as the primordial father of mankind and his relationship with the countless generations that followed his existence, elevated through Alaya’s integration into a phenomenon capable of extending protection across the collective foundation of Human Order. Although Adam’s legend establishes him as humanity’s progenitor, the meaning of this skill is not limited to biological descent or the transmission of inherited characteristics. Rather, it represents the spiritual relationship between the first human and the continued existence of mankind as a succession of individual lives, each possessing the possibility of developing independently of those who came before. Through this foundation, Adam-Alaya recognizes the preservation of humanity not merely as an abstract requirement imposed by Alaya’s collective survival imperative, but as an obligation toward the lives that constitute humanity itself. The skill consequently grants exceptional compatibility with defensive phenomena intended to preserve human existence, permitting Adam-Alaya to direct available Counter Force resources toward the protection of individuals, communities, and populations threatened by hostile supernatural interference. Its operation is not restricted to the immediate vicinity of his manifested body, as the connection with Alaya allows compatible interventions to be coordinated across the accessible Human Order foundation. When an attack threatens a population, Adam-Alaya may reinforce protective measures, strengthen the resistance of the affected human spiritual foundations, or coordinate the deployment of suitable agents to prevent further loss of life. The effectiveness of such intervention increases when the danger corresponds directly to a recognized existential threat to mankind, allowing the Counter Force to allocate resources according to the necessity of preserving humanity’s future. However, Father of Humanity is not simply a generalized defensive barrier, nor does it guarantee that every individual under Adam’s protection will survive. Its most distinctive property is the recognition of humanity without regard to the moral virtue, historical significance, or social position of the person being protected. A king possesses no greater claim to the skill’s fundamental recognition than a farmer, and an individual remembered as a villain does not cease to be human merely because of the crimes they have committed. Adam may condemn such actions, oppose their perpetrators, or recognize that an individual must be restrained or killed to prevent further suffering, but he does not permit the categorical denial of their humanity to become the basis of his judgment. This distinction is particularly important when the skill operates alongside Alaya’s utilitarian calculations, as the collective unconscious may determine that the loss of a smaller population is acceptable if it preserves humanity as a whole. Adam’s individual personality introduces an additional consideration: each life represents an existence whose experiences and possibilities cannot be completely represented by its numerical contribution to mankind’s survival. Consequently, he may attempt to allocate resources toward protecting individuals even when a purely impersonal intervention would disregard them, provided that doing so remains compatible with the Counter Force’s available resources and fundamental objective. The skill also strengthens his ability to recognize the vulnerability of human beings subjected to forced spiritual transformation, conceptual erasure, or externally imposed alterations of their identity, allowing the original foundation of humanity to serve as a protective reference against such interference. Nevertheless, Father of Humanity does not establish ownership over the people it protects, grant Adam unrestricted authority to command their decisions, or require that humanity remain forever dependent upon him. Its EX rank represents the extraordinary relationship between the first human’s parental identity and the collective will of his descendants to continue existing. Adam-Alaya does not protect mankind because he considers humanity his property. He protects it because each succeeding generation possesses the right to experience a future that he himself could never have known.

Paradise Lost (EX): A conceptual resistance ability born from Adam’s expulsion from Eden, representing the irrevocable transition between primordial existence within paradise and the mortal human condition that followed the acquisition of knowledge and the experience of the Fall. While the Garden of Eden constitutes an extraordinary Mystery within Adam’s legend, the significance of Paradise Lost derives not from his ability to recreate its original state, but from the fact that he has already experienced the loss of that state and continued living beyond it. The skill therefore embodies a fundamental principle concerning humanity’s relationship with the ideal: the existence of paradise does not necessarily establish that mankind must remain within it, and the removal of suffering does not automatically justify the elimination of individuality, choice, or the capacity for further development. Within the supernatural framework of Adam-Alaya, this principle manifests as exceptional resistance against phenomena that attempt to impose a permanent condition of perfection upon humanity through the suppression of its independent future. Artificial worlds in which human beings are prevented from changing, civilizations preserved indefinitely by the destruction of personal freedom, and supernatural systems that maintain happiness through the compulsory elimination of suffering may encounter resistance from Paradise Lost when their underlying conditions amount to the stagnation or invalidation of human existence. The skill operates by recognizing the distinction between a world in which humanity can freely pursue happiness and a world in which happiness has been imposed as an unalterable condition. Through Alaya’s collective awareness, Adam-Alaya can extend this recognition beyond the circumstances of individual spiritual interference, allowing him to identify large-scale systems whose apparent benevolence conceals the permanent restriction of mankind’s development. It is especially effective when confronting an imposed Texture, bounded world, artificial historical foundation, or supernatural paradise that sustains itself by denying its inhabitants the possibility of meaningful change. In such circumstances, Paradise Lost may protect Adam’s consciousness against conceptual assimilation and reinforce his ability to distinguish the original human spiritual foundation from the externally imposed condition. When combined with Knowledge of Good and Evil, the skill permits him to evaluate whether the preservation offered by such a system is genuinely compatible with mankind’s continued existence as humanity, while Primordial Covenant may coordinate defensive intervention against the mechanism sustaining the imposed state. The skill does not, however, automatically invalidate every utopia, eliminate every form of immortality, or permit Adam to destroy any peaceful civilization merely because its inhabitants have achieved a condition resembling paradise. Nor does it represent an intrinsic hostility toward divine salvation or the possibility of genuine happiness. Adam does not consider suffering necessary for human worth, and he would not condemn a world simply because its inhabitants no longer experience hardship. The decisive distinction is whether the condition preserves humanity’s capacity to exist and develop through its own will, or whether it has replaced that capacity with a state imposed by an external authority. Furthermore, Paradise Lost does not permit Adam-Alaya to nullify every temporal loop, dismantle every Reality Marble, or escape every supernatural prison through conceptual superiority alone. Its effectiveness depends upon the relationship between the target phenomenon and the specific Mystery of humanity’s lost paradise. The EX designation reflects the exceptional spiritual significance of an individual who experienced the original paradise and subsequently became the progenitor of humanity outside it. Adam-Alaya remembers Eden, but he does not regard the recovery of paradise as an objective worth sacrificing his descendants’ freedom to achieve. In his understanding, the value of humanity lies not in returning eternally to the place where its history began, but in possessing the possibility of continuing beyond that beginning.

Collective Experience of Mankind (EX): An extraordinary cognitive Personal Skill manifested through the integration of Alaya’s collective unconscious with Adam’s individual consciousness, granting access to the accumulated patterns of human experience preserved within the collective foundation of mankind. Unlike ordinary forms of clairvoyance, divine wisdom, or direct access to the memories of a particular individual, Collective Experience of Mankind functions through the recognition and interpretation of knowledge, behaviors, instincts, and methods developed through humanity’s historical existence. The experiences of countless generations have contributed to the evolution of human understanding, producing an immense accumulation of knowledge concerning survival, warfare, craftsmanship, medicine, agriculture, engineering, culture, philosophy, political organization, and the countless other disciplines through which mankind has adapted to its environment. Through Alaya, these accumulated patterns become accessible to Adam-Alaya as an integrated cognitive foundation, enabling him to evaluate circumstances using a breadth of experience that no ordinary individual could acquire within a single lifetime. His consciousness does not continuously receive the complete private memories of every human being who has ever existed, as such an arrangement would neither accurately represent the collective unconscious nor remain compatible with his individual personality. Instead, his Grand Saint Graph organizes relevant collective information into comprehensible forms, permitting Adam to draw upon established methods, recognize recurring patterns, and apply the appropriate knowledge without being overwhelmed by its quantity. In combat, the skill provides extraordinary analytical adaptability. A martial technique encountered for the first time may nevertheless resemble patterns preserved in the accumulated experience of human warfare, allowing Adam-Alaya to recognize its tactical principles even if he has never personally practiced the corresponding discipline. A weapon employing unfamiliar engineering may be evaluated through comparison with previously established technological concepts, while the strategic behavior of an opponent may be interpreted through the accumulated historical understanding of conflict, deception, leadership, and survival. When an enemy demonstrates an ability that lies beyond established human knowledge, the skill does not automatically reveal its true mechanism, but it may permit Adam-Alaya to formulate hypotheses and identify methods of investigation far more rapidly than would ordinarily be possible. The information obtained can also be incorporated into Primordial Covenant, permitting the results of failed defensive interventions to inform subsequent operations. This produces a reciprocal relationship between humanity’s accumulated knowledge and the Counter Force’s active attempts to preserve its future, with Adam’s individual judgment determining how the information should be interpreted and applied. The skill is particularly formidable when combined with True Name Discernment, as the recognition of an enemy’s historical or spiritual foundation may provide the context necessary to select effective strategies, or with Thronus Resonans, whose Spectral Servant formations can be organized according to the conceptual compatibility between their Noble Phantasms and the designated target. Nevertheless, Collective Experience of Mankind does not grant the automatic possession of every Heroic Spirit’s unique Skills, the unrestricted reproduction of Divine Constructs, or complete knowledge of phenomena that humanity has never encountered or recorded. The accumulated experiences of mankind may also contain contradictions, errors, obsolete assumptions, and incomplete interpretations, all of which must be evaluated rather than blindly accepted. Its EX designation therefore represents the impossibility of reducing collective human experience to an ordinary intellectual parameter, not the absolute completeness of the knowledge it provides. Adam-Alaya is extraordinarily difficult to outmaneuver through conventional human strategies because his judgment is informed by the lessons of countless generations. Yet he remains capable of encountering the genuinely unknown, and his greatest intellectual strength lies in the ability to recognize that even humanity’s accumulated experience is not equivalent to possessing every answer.

The Unconscious Will to Survive (EX): The supreme passive Personal Skill of Adam-Alaya, representing the direct incorporation of Alaya’s fundamental survival imperative into the spiritual and instinctive functions of the primordial human, and constituting the clearest expression of the difference between an ordinary Grand Servant and a conscious manifestation of the Counter Force. Alaya is not ordinarily characterized by deliberate individual judgment or conventional emotion, but by the collective unconscious desire of humanity to avoid extinction, a defensive impulse that may produce intervention whenever circumstances threaten mankind’s continued existence. Through Adam-Alaya’s composite Saint Graph, this collective impulse becomes an inherent property of his manifested existence, allowing the recognition of danger and the initiation of suitable defensive responses to occur without requiring Adam to consciously deliberate upon every hostile phenomenon. The skill operates continuously, receiving information from the threat-recognition mechanisms of Human Order and comparing disturbances against the conditions that permit humanity to survive. When an event is recognized as a sufficiently significant danger, the relevant defensive functions may begin operating before Adam’s conscious awareness has completed its interpretation of the situation. An attack approaching his spiritual body may provoke automatic reinforcement of the Saint Graph, an unforeseen danger to a protected human population may initiate emergency intervention, and a hostile phenomenon compromising the surrounding Human Order foundation may trigger defensive regulation before Adam has deliberately activated Primordial Covenant. This responsiveness is particularly extraordinary because the Counter Force’s perception is not restricted to Adam’s physical senses. A hostile action occurring beyond his field of vision may still be recognized through its relationship with Human Order, while an attack that exceeds his ordinary Agility may encounter defenses initiated through collective threat perception rather than conventional bodily reaction. Furthermore, the skill permits multiple defensive processes to operate concurrently, meaning that Adam-Alaya can continue fighting, communicating, or exercising personal judgment while Alaya initiates responses to other recognized dangers. Its highest expression occurs when a battle presents a genuine extinction-level threat, under which circumstances the urgency of humanity’s collective survival can justify extraordinary Counter Force reinforcement. If a defensive measure fails, the skill can preserve the relevant information and contribute to the selection of another response, establishing a persistent cycle of recognition, intervention, assessment, and renewed resistance. Nevertheless, this process should not be mistaken for unrestricted adaptation or absolute invulnerability. The Counter Force cannot respond effectively to a threat it cannot recognize, nor can it guarantee an appropriate defense against a phenomenon operating beyond its available resources and conceptual jurisdiction. An attack capable of bypassing the foundational conditions through which Alaya recognizes danger may reach Adam-Alaya before the system can respond, while an extraordinarily powerful opponent may overwhelm several defensive layers simultaneously. The skill also possesses an important relationship with Adam’s individual consciousness. Although unconscious defensive measures may begin automatically, decisions requiring deliberate moral judgment, exceptional administrative authorization, or the activation of catastrophic Noble Phantasms remain subject to the restrictions governing those powers. Alaya’s survival instinct cannot simply erase Adam’s personality and convert him into an unthinking instrument whenever a more efficient intervention becomes available. The distinction is essential, for the extraordinary defensive system operating within Adam-Alaya possesses a purpose rather than an independent personal will, while Adam possesses the responsibility of deciding how that purpose should be fulfilled. In ordinary combat, this makes him exceptionally difficult to surprise or overwhelm, since an enemy may find that defensive mechanisms have already begun operating before Adam visibly reacts. In a battle threatening the extinction of humanity, the skill becomes still more formidable, allowing the full urgency of mankind’s collective desire to survive to express itself through the Grand Ruler’s spiritual foundation. Its EX designation represents not an ability to survive every conceivable phenomenon, but the direct manifestation of humanity’s primordial refusal to cease existing. So long as Alaya remains capable of recognizing the danger and possesses the resources to act, the destruction of one defensive response does not necessarily signify the end of the struggle. Humanity may continue resisting through Adam-Alaya, even when an ordinary Servant would have already exhausted every means of survival.

NOBLE PHANTASM 
Adamah Genesis — The Garden Where the First Breath Was Given. Rank: EX. Classification: Anti-Genesis. Range: 200. Maximum Targets: 1,000. is the first Noble Phantasm possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya, an extraordinary Anti-Genesis phenomenon derived from the primordial Mystery of Adam’s creation and his existence within the Garden of Eden before the Fall of Man. Unlike conventional Noble Phantasms that crystallize the achievements, weapons, legends, or defining historical accomplishments of an individual Heroic Spirit, Adamah Genesis embodies the circumstances through which the first human came into existence, reproducing the spiritual relationship between primordial matter, divine creation, and the emergence of human individuality. Its foundation originates from Adam’s formation from the dust of the earth and the reception of the divine breath through which he became a living being, an event that possesses an exceptional position within the Abrahamic creation traditions constituting his spiritual foundation. In the supernatural framework of Adam-Alaya, this Mystery is not interpreted as an Authority granting Adam the right to create existence from absolute nothingness, for such an act would belong to the Creator rather than the being who received life. Instead, the Noble Phantasm manifests the conditions through which an existence passes from its original foundation into a subsequently established form, permitting Adam-Alaya to recognize and interfere with the conceptual process of formation itself. Upon activation, Adam-Alaya establishes a primordial Reality Marble corresponding to Eden, the original paradise in which mankind existed before the emergence of its recorded historical development. The surrounding environment is overwritten by a spiritual landscape whose structure reflects the Garden of Eden, characterized by fertile earth, flowing rivers, an atmosphere possessing extraordinary purity, and an underlying Mystery associated with the original condition of human existence. Yet the resulting domain is not merely an artificial paradise intended to preserve life or reproduce a perfect natural environment. It is an exceptional spiritual territory in which the distinction between an entity’s original foundation and the conditions responsible for its subsequent manifestation becomes unusually pronounced. Within this domain, phenomena that ordinarily appear as completed existences may be recognized according to the sequences of creation, transformation, and establishment through which their present forms were produced. A spiritual construct sustained through magecraft may be perceived as an arrangement of magical energy and conceptual instructions, an artificial life-form may be recognized according to the materials and principles responsible for its construction, and an imposed supernatural phenomenon may have the foundation supporting its manifestation exposed to Adam-Alaya’s perception. The central ability of Adamah Genesis is therefore designated Conceptual Regression of Creation, a process through which Adam-Alaya may interfere with the transition between an existence’s foundational state and the completed condition it currently occupies. Rather than merely inflicting damage upon the target, the Noble Phantasm attempts to reverse or invalidate the conditions responsible for its formation, causing the affected existence to regress toward a prior conceptual foundation. A weapon produced through artificial spiritual construction may lose the magical arrangement that allows it to maintain its form, a bounded field may be reduced toward the principles and energy from which it was assembled, and an artificial incarnation may find the distinction between its original spiritual information and its manifested body forcibly exposed. In more extraordinary circumstances, the Noble Phantasm may attack the conceptual foundation through which a supernatural entity acquired its current existence, effectively opposing the act of genesis responsible for its manifestation rather than attempting to destroy the manifestation through conventional means. This distinction is what establishes the Noble Phantasm’s Anti-Genesis classification, for its destructive principle does not concern the amount of physical matter it can annihilate, but the extent to which it can interfere with the conceptual process through which something came into being. Its greatest effectiveness is therefore demonstrated against existences whose present forms are dependent upon identifiable conditions of creation, particularly artificial life, magical constructs, summoned spiritual bodies, and supernatural environments sustained through imposed foundations. Against beings whose existence is self-sustaining, whose origins are inaccessible to Adam’s primordial Mystery, or whose nature possesses a foundation superior to the conceptual jurisdiction of Eden, the Noble Phantasm may be unable to establish a meaningful regression. An entity possessing an extraordinary Divine Authority, a fundamentally extraterrestrial spiritual constitution, or a mode of existence independent of the processes recognized by the domain cannot automatically be returned to nothingness merely because Adam-Alaya possesses an Anti-Genesis Noble Phantasm. The operation is also distinct from ordinary temporal reversal, as Adamah Genesis does not necessarily return the world to an earlier chronological moment. Instead, it attacks the conceptual relationship between the original and completed states of an existence, allowing the foundation of a phenomenon to be challenged without requiring the literal reversal of every event responsible for its creation. The manifestation of Eden also possesses an exceptional relationship with Adam-Alaya’s Personal Skills, particularly Primordial Human, Breath of Life, and Imposition of Names. Because the Reality Marble reproduces the circumstances of Adam’s primordial existence, his spiritual foundation achieves a greater degree of correspondence with its original condition, strengthening the restorative process through which his damaged manifestation may be reconstructed. Likewise, the conceptual distinctions revealed within Eden improve the accuracy of Imposition of Names, permitting Adam-Alaya to distinguish between an entity’s essential nature and the artificial characteristics imposed upon it. Through the integration of Alaya, these properties acquire an additional administrative function, allowing the Counter Force’s recognition and defensive mechanisms to operate in conjunction with the primordial domain. A hostile phenomenon attempting to overwrite Human Order may therefore encounter not only the defensive correction of Alaya, but also a spiritual environment capable of exposing and destabilizing the process through which the hostile foundation was imposed. This relationship makes Adamah Genesis particularly effective against artificial worlds, false paradises, and supernatural systems attempting to establish an incompatible order upon the human world, although the Noble Phantasm cannot automatically invalidate every independent Texture or higher-order metaphysical foundation. Its manifestation also presents an extraordinary conceptual relationship with Avicebron’s Golem Keter Malkuth, whose autonomous Reality Marble attempts to reproduce the primordial human Adam and transform its surroundings into Eden. Whereas Avicebron’s creation represents an artificial recreation of the original human and the paradise associated with his existence, Adamah Genesis derives directly from the primordial spiritual foundation that such a recreation attempts to imitate. The distinction is one of conceptual authenticity rather than an unconditional guarantee of victory, for even a more authentic Mystery may encounter unfavorable conditions or an opponent possessing extraordinary power. Nevertheless, the existence of Adamah Genesis represents a fundamental difference between an artificial construct aspiring toward the recreation of paradise and the original human whose spiritual foundation preserves the Mystery of having existed within it. Its EX rank reflects the impossibility of measuring the conceptual regression of creation through ordinary destructive parameters, for an attack capable of reducing a vast artificial spiritual structure to its original foundation may require less direct physical force than one capable of demolishing a comparatively small but fundamentally independent existence. Despite its extraordinary potential, Adamah Genesis remains restricted by the distinction between the Creator and the created. Adam-Alaya does not possess the right to recreate God’s original act of creation without limitation, cannot arbitrarily erase every existence through a declaration of primordial superiority, and cannot extend the authority of his Reality Marble beyond the metaphysical conditions supporting its operation. Furthermore, the manifestation of Eden requires the expenditure of magical energy and the maintenance of an imposed internal world, making it susceptible to interference from sufficiently powerful external authorities or phenomena capable of overwhelming its foundation. The Noble Phantasm’s significance is consequently both metaphysical and philosophical. It represents the extraordinary Mystery of humanity’s first existence, but also the inability of the First Human to become the Creator merely because he remembers the circumstances of his own creation. For Adam-Alaya, the Garden of Eden is neither a lost kingdom to be conquered again nor a paradise he wishes to impose upon his descendants. It is the spiritual memory of humanity’s beginning, transformed into a weapon capable of opposing the conditions through which hostile existences are brought into the world. Adamah Genesis is therefore the manifestation of the First Human’s relationship with creation: a Noble Phantasm that does not simply destroy what exists, but challenges the act through which that existence became possible.

II. Alaya Humanitas: Humanity Shall See Another Tomorrow — Rank: EX. Classification: Anti-Threat-to-Humanity. Range: 1–1000 Maximum Targets: Unlimited. is the second Noble Phantasm possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya and the supreme defensive manifestation of his composite spiritual foundation, representing the collective unconscious desire of humanity to avoid extinction elevated into an extraordinary Counter Force intervention. Unlike Adamah Genesis, whose Mystery originates from the primordial existence of Adam, Alaya Humanitas derives directly from Alaya, the human component of the Counter Force, and constitutes the most complete expression of mankind’s unconscious determination to preserve its own future. The Noble Phantasm is founded upon a principle that precedes the ambitions of individual civilizations, the authority of kings, and the achievements of Heroic Spirits: humanity possesses a collective desire to continue existing, and that desire has established defensive mechanisms capable of responding to circumstances threatening its survival. Under ordinary conditions, the Counter Force acts without possessing the personality or moral judgment of an individual human being, intervening through indirect alterations in circumstances, the empowerment of suitable agents, or the deployment of Heroic Spirits and Counter Guardians when less direct measures prove insufficient. Alaya Humanitas represents the exceptional transformation of this impersonal defensive process into a Noble Phantasm consciously administered through Adam, whose individual spiritual foundation has become directly integrated with the collective unconscious responsible for the interventions. Its activation does not produce a single predetermined offensive phenomenon, nor does it necessarily manifest as a barrier, weapon, or conventional field of magical energy. Rather, the Noble Phantasm establishes a comprehensive defensive operation through which the accessible resources of Alaya are concentrated upon the preservation of humanity against a recognized existential threat. The first stage of this operation consists of Existential Threat Recognition, whereby Adam-Alaya identifies the mechanism through which the designated phenomenon threatens the continuation of mankind and incorporates that mechanism into the Counter Force’s defensive assessment. The evaluation does not depend exclusively upon an opponent’s individual combat parameters, the destructive output of its attacks, or the degree of Mystery associated with its existence. Instead, the Counter Force evaluates the danger according to its potential consequences for humanity, meaning that a comparatively weak supernatural phenomenon capable of initiating mankind’s extinction may provoke an extraordinary response, while an immensely powerful entity whose actions do not endanger Human Order may receive little reason for equivalent intervention. Once a threat has been sufficiently recognized, Alaya Humanitas initiates Total Defensive Mobilization, a state in which the Counter Force’s available functions may be coordinated through Adam-Alaya’s Grand Saint Graph as parts of a single operation. Protective measures can be reinforced, compatible Counter Guardians can be deployed, suitable Heroic Spirit records can be selected, hostile magical phenomena can be suppressed, and the foundations of Human Order can be strengthened against interference. At the same time, Alaya’s indirect intervention mechanisms may influence the circumstances surrounding the threat, creating opportunities for survival or disrupting conditions necessary for the completion of an otherwise catastrophic action. The Noble Phantasm therefore does not merely increase Adam-Alaya’s magical energy output, but permits him to coordinate multiple layers of defensive intervention whose combined effects may extend far beyond the immediate battlefield. Against a localized existential danger, this may manifest as the reinforcement of a particular region or the deployment of specialized guardians, while an event threatening the entire planetary Human Order foundation may justify an operation extending across the relevant portions of the world and its associated historical continuity. The maximum extent of the intervention is not determined by a fixed physical radius, but by the relationship between the recognized threat, the available resources of Alaya, and the capacity of Adam-Alaya’s Saint Graph to administer the corresponding defensive processes. This distinction makes Alaya Humanitas fundamentally different from conventional large-scale Noble Phantasms, for its greatest power is not the destruction of a particular area, but the establishment of a coordinated survival response whose scale corresponds to the nature of the catastrophe. The Noble Phantasm’s most extraordinary property is Recursive Defensive Escalation, an adaptive mechanism through which the results of previous interventions are incorporated into subsequent Counter Force operations. If an opponent destroys a defensive barrier, the method through which that barrier was overcome may become the subject of further analysis. If a deployed Counter Guardian is defeated, the information obtained from that defeat may assist in selecting another agent whose abilities are more compatible with the threat. If an enemy possesses a conceptual weapon capable of bypassing conventional durability, Adam-Alaya may attempt to employ defensive methods that do not rely upon the same compromised principle. Through Collective Experience of Mankind, this process can draw upon the accumulated tactical knowledge and practical understanding developed throughout human history, allowing new observations to be interpreted through the collective experience of countless generations. The resulting phenomenon resembles a continuously evolving defensive strategy rather than unrestricted supernatural adaptation, as the Counter Force must still possess a viable method of intervention and sufficient resources to execute it. Alaya Humanitas cannot automatically generate an ability that has no foundation within the possibilities available to Human Order, nor does repeated observation guarantee that an incomprehensible enemy will eventually become vulnerable. Nevertheless, the effectiveness of an opponent’s initial strategy may diminish over the course of an engagement if Adam-Alaya remains capable of assessing its mechanisms and deploying alternative responses. The danger presented by this Noble Phantasm is therefore cumulative: destroying one defensive measure does not necessarily eliminate the system responsible for generating the next. Moreover, the Noble Phantasm can maintain several operations simultaneously, allowing Adam-Alaya to continue fighting personally while defensive resources are allocated to distant locations, compatible guardians are mobilized, and the surrounding Human Order foundation is reinforced against further interference. Its relationship with the other Noble Phantasms is similarly significant. Adamah Genesis may be employed when a recognized threat possesses an artificial foundation susceptible to conceptual regression, while Thronus Resonans allows the Counter Force’s assessment to be translated into immediate offensive deployments involving complete Heroic Spirit records. The resulting arrangement permits Adam-Alaya to select different forms of intervention according to their compatibility with the threat rather than relying upon a single predetermined form of attack. However, the catastrophic powers of Mors Terrae and Thronus Ultimus remain subject to their own exceptional conditions and cannot be treated as ordinary components of an automatically escalating response. The destruction of portions of Earth’s remaining lifespan or the termination of the Throne of Heroes requires considerations extending beyond the immediate elimination of an enemy, and Adam’s individual judgment remains indispensable to those decisions. Indeed, the most important characteristic of Alaya Humanitas lies in the contrast between its collective foundation and the personality through which it is exercised. Alaya’s unconscious survival imperative may identify a solution that preserves the greatest possible proportion of humanity while sacrificing a comparatively small number of individuals, but Adam does not necessarily regard such an outcome as morally sufficient merely because it fulfills the underlying objective. He possesses the capacity to consider the lives affected by an intervention, search for alternative methods, and refuse actions whose consequences he cannot accept, even when the Counter Force’s assessment identifies them as efficient. This does not permit Adam to demand unlimited resources for actions unrelated to humanity’s preservation, nor does it eliminate the automatic defensive processes inherent to Alaya, but it creates an unprecedented distinction between the objective of the collective unconscious and the individual judgment responsible for directing its extraordinary power. The Noble Phantasm’s EX rank consequently reflects not only its vast operational scale, but the abnormal relationship between an individual Servant and the survival mechanisms of an entire species. Against an ordinary opponent, the majority of its extraordinary functions may remain unnecessary, and the Counter Force may refuse to allocate resources disproportionate to the danger. Against a genuine threat of human extinction, however, Alaya Humanitas can become one of the most formidable defensive operations conceivable within Human Order, coordinating circumstances, agents, historical foundations, and Heroic Spirit records in a collective attempt to prevent mankind’s disappearance. Yet even such an intervention cannot guarantee victory against every conceivable existence, for Alaya possesses neither absolute omniscience nor unlimited authority over the Root, Gaia, or every phenomenon originating beyond the human world. Alaya Humanitas is the Noble Phantasm through which humanity’s refusal to perish becomes an organized act of resistance, and through which the First Human consciously directs the collective will of his descendants toward the preservation of another tomorrow.

III. Mors Terrae: The Golden Excision of Earth’s Final Day — Rank: EX. Classification: Anti-Earth. Range: 1–1000 Maximum Targets: 1. Is the third Noble Phantasm possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya, an extraordinary Anti-Earth phenomenon embodying the most destructive contradiction inherent in humanity’s collective survival instinct: the willingness of mankind to consume the very world sustaining its existence in order to ensure its own preservation. Unlike conventional Anti-Planet Noble Phantasms, whose destructive significance is generally associated with their capacity to devastate or annihilate celestial bodies, Mors Terrae does not seek to destroy Earth in its entirety, nor does it attempt to overcome the planet through a conventional application of superior destructive force. Instead, it exploits the finite continuation of Earth’s own existence as the conceptual foundation of an attack, extracting a designated portion of the planet’s eventual terminal condition and actualizing that portion prematurely upon an opponent whose ontological existence has been successfully bound to it. The underlying principle is expressed through an unusual relationship between individual existence and planetary containment. Although a being may possess an endless lifespan, an independent spiritual structure, or no inherent Concept of Death whatsoever, its continued existence may nevertheless occupy a particular position within the planetary framework of Earth, a greater existence whose own continuation is not without an eventual endpoint. Under ordinary metaphysical conditions, the fact that an individual exists within a finite world does not necessarily imply that the individual’s existence must terminate when that world reaches its end, particularly when the being possesses a foundation capable of sustaining itself independently of the planet. Mors Terrae deliberately establishes such a relationship as a binding conceptual phenomenon, converting the condition of existing within Earth’s ontological framework into a means through which the planet’s eventual termination may be imposed upon a designated constituent without directly modifying that constituent’s own mortality. The resulting attack is neither the imposition of a Concept of Death upon a deathless being nor the discovery of an otherwise concealed endpoint within an immortal existence. Rather, it is the premature actualization of a localized subsection of Earth’s own death, with the target eliminated because its existence has been designated as the constituent corresponding to that subsection. The Noble Phantasm therefore originates from an extraordinary interpretation of the relationship between Alaya and the planet sustaining humanity. Alaya represents mankind’s collective will to survive, while Gaia represents the preservation of Earth itself, and their objectives are not necessarily identical. Mors Terrae elevates that difference into a catastrophic weapon, permitting Adam-Alaya to consume portions of the planet’s remaining vitality in order to eliminate threats that would otherwise be capable of destroying humanity. Its activation begins when Adam-Alaya places his hand directly upon the ground, establishing contact with the planetary foundation and initiating a vast ritual circle composed of intricately layered magical formulae. The circle expands outward at a speed corresponding to Adam-Alaya’s thoughts, its circumference increasing according to the physical, spiritual, informational, or conceptual extent of the opponent selected for elimination. Unlike an ordinary magical formation whose size may be determined by the distance separating the caster from the target, the ritual of Mors Terrae attempts to establish a field sufficient to encompass the scale of the target’s relevant existence, meaning that a physically enormous being, an entity distributed through multiple interconnected manifestations, or an existence sustained through an extensive informational structure may require a considerably greater ritual manifestation than an individual possessing an ordinary localized body. The expansion itself is not the principal destructive action, but the process through which the required planetary foundation is established and the immense quantity of energy necessary for the Noble Phantasm is accumulated. Mors Terrae requires enormous concentrations of Grain, or True Ether, far beyond the reserves ordinarily available to a Servant, and the exceptional nature of its manifestation lies partly in the means through which those quantities are obtained. Rather than merely drawing upon already existing reserves of ambient magical energy, the ritual converts the resources of the living Earth into the required Grain-based medium, consuming the planet’s substance, atmosphere, and remaining vitality as the foundation for the operation. This process is an extraordinary original application of the Grain-related mysteries associated with the dead-Earth conditions of Notes., rather than an ordinary form of magecraft available to human magi. As the ritual circle expands, the surrounding terrain begins to deteriorate, geological structures lose portions of their physical and spiritual integrity, and the atmosphere becomes subject to the gradual extraction of the resources sustaining its present condition. More importantly, the ritual does not merely consume matter that the planet could otherwise replace through ordinary natural processes. It traces the continued existence of Earth itself and extracts the energetic equivalent of portions of the planet’s remaining lifespan, diminishing the future vitality available to the planetary foundation in order to prepare the Noble Phantasm’s final release. The phenomenon resembles the destructive methods through which humanity has historically secured its survival by exploiting the natural world, except that the resources being consumed are no longer limited to forests, minerals, oceans, or atmospheric conditions, but extend to the very continuation of Earth’s existence. For this reason, Mors Terrae has been described as a simple human consumption for humanity’s preservation, an expression of mankind’s capacity to exhaust its environment for survival elevated to a scale at which the planet’s own lifespan becomes the resource being expended. The ritual’s next operation is designated Planetary Terminal Tracing, through which Adam-Alaya establishes a relationship between the present Earth and the eventual termination of the relevant planetary existence. This does not require him to observe a complete predetermined future in which every historical event leading to Earth’s destruction has already been established, nor does it involve traveling to the distant future and retrieving a literal fragment of the planet’s ruined physical body. Rather, the ritual recognizes the terminal condition belonging to the finite continuation of Earth’s existence and treats that condition as a metaphysical whole whose actualization may be selectively divided through the operation of the Noble Phantasm. The distant end of Earth is therefore not reproduced as an entire chronological event, but used as the conceptual medium from which a localized terminal subsection may be isolated. Every existence occupying a place within Earth’s planetary framework can be understood as possessing a corresponding relationship with the world whose conditions permit that existence to remain present. Mors Terrae exploits this relationship through a conceptual analogy in which the world constitutes a vast canvas and the beings existing within it occupy individual portions of the image formed upon its surface. The eventual destruction of the entire canvas represents the termination of Earth’s existence, while a particular being constitutes a designated portion of the structure that would be lost when that ending occurs. The Noble Phantasm does not destroy the complete canvas. Instead, it identifies the exact portion corresponding to the intended target and cuts that portion away, removing the target together with an infinitesimal fragment of the world’s continued existence while permitting the remainder of Earth to continue toward its distant natural conclusion. The target is therefore not eliminated because its personal lifespan has ended, but because the portion of Earth’s eventual ending assigned to its ontological existence has been made to occur ahead of the rest of the planet. In order to establish the necessary correspondence, Adam-Alaya must first execute an indispensable targeting operation known as the Tracer Round, which is initiated through the invocation of the Noble Phantasm’s True Name and functions as the means through which the intended opponent is designated as a constituent of Earth’s terminal event. The Tracer Round is not merely a projectile intended to strike the physical location occupied by the target, nor does it simply establish a conventional magical lock capable of following an opponent through space. Instead, it must successfully reach and establish contact with the target’s ontological foundation, identifying the existence itself as occupying a particular position within the planetary framework. Once the designation has been completed, a flame-like golden spiral manifests upon the target’s very being, an extraordinary conceptual inscription known as the Immutable Golden Spiral. This spiral is not fundamentally attached to the opponent’s skin, physical body, spiritual vessel, or informational avatar, although it may become visible upon any of those manifestations. It is engraved upon the ontological identity through which the target exists within Earth, establishing a fixed correspondence between that existence and the precise subsection of the planet’s eventual death selected for premature actualization. Its manifestation indicates that the Tracer Round has successfully designated the target and that the conceptual relationship necessary for the final attack has become established. The spiral does not impose a finite lifespan upon an immortal opponent, grant a Concept of Death to an entity lacking one, or overwrite an existing principle of deathlessness. Instead, it declares that the selected existence occupies the particular portion of Earth’s terminal event that will now be actualized, allowing the Noble Phantasm to bypass the question of whether the target possesses an individual death at all. Once the Immutable Golden Spiral has been established, its designation cannot be evaded through ordinary changes in physical position, form, or manifestation, because the attack is no longer directed toward the coordinates occupied by a body, but toward the ontological existence identified by the completed mark. A being that abandons its physical vessel, becomes intangible, transfers itself into a compatible digital structure, assumes an informational existence, or moves through a dimension belonging to Earth’s planetary framework remains subject to the designation so long as the same marked existence continues to occupy that framework. Even an entity composed entirely of information, or one whose spiritual structure cannot be assigned a conventional finite lifespan, remains vulnerable if its actual existence is contained within the jurisdiction upon which Mors Terrae operates. The distinction becomes especially significant against beings possessing no inherent Concept of Death, for such entities would ordinarily be unaffected by abilities that depend upon identifying, imposing, or actualizing their personal mortality. Mors Terrae does not attempt any of those operations. It uses Earth’s own eventual death as the terminal event and makes the target’s continued existence a designated subsection of that event. Thus, the individual may remain deathless according to its own spiritual constitution while nevertheless being eliminated through the premature ending of the portion of Earth to which it has been bound. The completed designation also establishes the Noble Phantasm’s exceptional accuracy. Prior to the successful application of the Tracer Round, an opponent may evade the designation, interrupt the ritual, or prevent the necessary correspondence from being formed. Once the Immutable Golden Spiral has been successfully established and the target remains within the applicable planetary framework, however, the final strike possesses an ontologically fixed destination that cannot be avoided through conventional movement, instantaneous relocation within Earth’s associated dimensions, or the abandonment of a temporary body. The attack is guaranteed to reach the designated existence because its destination is no longer a physical point in space, but the particular subsection of Earth’s terminal condition that has been assigned to the target. This does not make the entire Noble Phantasm impossible to interrupt, as the ritual still requires sufficient planetary resources and the completion of its release sequence, but it renders ordinary evasion ineffective after the necessary designation has been established. Once the ritual circle has accumulated the required Grain and the planetary terminal subsection has been prepared, a colossal magical formation manifests high in satellite orbit above Earth, functioning as the final release structure through which the accumulated energy and conceptual terminal condition are actualized. The orbital formation appears as an immense golden ritual array whose inscriptions correspond to the relationship between Earth’s continuing existence and the designated fragment of its eventual ending. Upon Adam-Alaya’s command, the formation releases a concentrated golden radiance that descends toward the Immutable Golden Spiral, producing an attack whose visible appearance resembles an overwhelming orbital bombardment but whose actual mechanism is not dependent upon conventional destructive energy. The golden light is the perceptible manifestation of a terminal event being forcibly actualized, its path determined by the ontological correspondence established through the Tracer Round rather than the ordinary mechanics of a projectile traveling toward a physical target. At the moment of release, observers may witness brief distortions in the surrounding environment corresponding to the terminal condition of Earth’s existence. These phenomena are not necessarily literal images of the complete astronomical or historical sequence through which the planet will eventually meet its end, but genuine perceptual consequences of a localized portion of that ending becoming actual within the present. The sky may appear to lose the properties associated with a living world, the surrounding space may momentarily resemble a region whose continued existence has already concluded, and the boundary between the still-living Earth and the designated terminal subsection may become visible as a contradiction between two states of planetary existence. To ordinary observers, the event may resemble a golden flash accompanied by the sudden disappearance of an enemy, but beings possessing sufficiently advanced spiritual, conceptual, or planetary perception may recognize something far more disturbing: they are witnessing a tiny portion of Earth’s eventual death occurring billions of years before the remainder of the planet reaches its conclusion. When the orbital light reaches the Immutable Golden Spiral, the designated terminal subsection is actualized immediately. The target’s continued existence is excised together with the corresponding fragment of Earth’s ontological framework, leaving a small, gaping void where the affected existence previously occupied the world. This void is not merely the physical absence of a destroyed body, but the residual indication that a portion of the planet’s continued existence has already reached its endpoint. The remainder of Earth continues to exist, yet the fragment corresponding to the target has permanently departed from the world’s ongoing condition. In this manner, Mors Terrae can eliminate beings whose own mortality is absent, because it does not require the target’s personal existence to possess an endpoint. The finite continuation of the planetary framework supplies the terminal condition, while the Immutable Golden Spiral establishes the otherwise nonexistent relationship necessary to apply that condition to the target. This is also why the Noble Phantasm is classified as Anti-Earth rather than Anti-Planet. Its objective is not to overwhelm the defensive mechanisms of Earth through the external application of force sufficient to destroy the celestial body, but to weaponize a fragment of the planet’s own terminal condition against an existence contained within it. The completed strike therefore circumvents the ordinary defensive distinction between an external attack attempting to destroy Earth and the eventual death belonging to Earth’s own existence, since the event being actualized is derived from the planetary foundation itself. Gaia may oppose the preparation of the ritual, resist the consumption of planetary resources, or interfere with the process before the necessary conditions have been established, but the completed ontological designation does not function as an ordinary external assault that must simply overpower Earth’s planetary defenses. Nevertheless, the Noble Phantasm’s jurisdiction is not unlimited. A being whose actual foundation exists entirely outside Earth and whose presence within the planetary framework consists only of an independently sustained projection may not be eliminated in its entirety merely because that projection is successfully marked; the attack can only excise the existence genuinely incorporated into the applicable planetary subsection. Likewise, the successful establishment of the Immutable Golden Spiral is indispensable, and the ritual cannot guarantee an attack against a target that has never been ontologically designated. Its enormous consumption of planetary resources also represents a catastrophic limitation, as every activation diminishes a genuine portion of Earth’s remaining vitality, inflicting damage upon the world that cannot simply be dismissed as an illusion or ordinary expenditure of replaceable magical energy. This is particularly significant because Adam-Alaya exists to preserve humanity, whose continued existence ordinarily depends upon the very planet being consumed. The greater the threat and the more extensive the target’s ontological existence, the greater the expenditure potentially required to eliminate it, creating circumstances in which the Counter Force must determine whether the loss of a portion of Earth’s distant future is justified by the preservation of humanity’s immediate one. For Adam, whose individual consciousness remains dominant despite his integration with Alaya, the philosophical consequences of this decision are inescapable. The primordial human who was formed from the dust of the earth possesses a weapon capable of consuming the lifespan of the world from which he originated, sacrificing a fragment of its eventual ending to preserve the descendants who followed him. Mors Terrae is therefore both an extraordinary offensive Noble Phantasm and a condemnation of the destructive tendencies inherent in humanity’s historical relationship with its environment. Its greatest horror lies not merely in the elimination of beings that possess no personal death, but in the fact that the act of eliminating them is accomplished by bringing a portion of Earth’s own death into the present. Mors Terrae does not grant death to the deathless. It makes a fragment of Earth’s death happen where the deathless being exists, cutting that existence from the world’s continuing reality while the remainder of the planet is left to survive its own prematurely diminished future.

IV. Thronus Ultimus: The Throne Where No Hero Shall Be Called Again — Rank: EX. Classification: Anti-Throne of Heroes. Range: 1–1000 Maximum Targets: 1000. Is the fourth Noble Phantasm possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya, an extraordinary Anti-Throne of Heroes phenomenon representing the ultimate emergency authority of the Counter Force over the spiritual recording system through which humanity’s Heroic Spirits are preserved and summoned. Unlike conventional Noble Phantasms whose destructive effects are directed against physical targets, spiritual bodies, bounded territories, or the surrounding world, Thronus Ultimus is an administrative and conceptual termination mechanism whose designated target is the higher-dimensional foundation sustaining the records of Heroic Spirits themselves. The Throne of Heroes is ordinarily understood as a domain existing outside conventional chronological time, where the records of individuals who have achieved sufficient significance are preserved independently of the historical eras in which they originally lived. Through appropriate summoning systems, portions of these records may be manifested as Servants, allowing heroes whose lives have already concluded to participate in events belonging to different historical periods. For Human Order, the existence of this repository constitutes an extraordinary defensive advantage, as the accumulated achievements, legends, and supernatural powers of humanity’s greatest individuals can be summoned to oppose dangers that later generations may be incapable of overcoming through their own immediate resources. Yet the existence of such a system also creates a profound vulnerability: if an enemy acquires the means to exploit the Heroic Spirit records or reproduce the mechanisms through which they are summoned, the defensive achievements of mankind may become instruments of its own destruction. The unprecedented precedent established by ORT, whose assimilation of Servant information permitted the construction of an extraordinary Grand Foreigner manifestation, revealed the possibility that an entity operating entirely outside humanity’s historical foundations could exploit the heroic system for purposes fundamentally incompatible with Human Order. Thronus Ultimus represents Alaya’s most catastrophic answer to that possibility, an emergency measure incorporated into Adam-Alaya’s Grand Saint Graph to ensure that the continued existence of the Throne of Heroes would not become an unavoidable cause of humanity’s extinction. The Noble Phantasm is consequently founded upon a paradox that would ordinarily be unacceptable to the Counter Force: the defensive system established to preserve humanity may, under sufficiently extraordinary conditions, require its own destruction in order to fulfill the purpose for which it exists. Unlike a conventional anti-summoning ability that interferes with a Servant’s manifested body or disrupts the magical energy sustaining a particular contract, Thronus Ultimus possesses the capacity to intervene against the underlying spiritual recording and summoning framework itself. Its operation is made possible through the direct integration of Alaya into Adam’s spiritual foundation, allowing the Grand Ruler to exercise exceptional administrative jurisdiction over the relationship between Human Order and its accumulated Heroic Spirit records. This does not imply that Adam personally created the Throne, that the Throne is an ordinary bounded field within his ownership, or that he possesses unrestricted sovereignty over every higher-dimensional spiritual existence. Rather, the unprecedented Grand Saint Graph provides an exceptional mechanism through which the Counter Force can initiate a system-level intervention against the heroic repository when its continued operation has become a direct existential danger to mankind. The Noble Phantasm possesses two principal degrees of release, the first being Archive Excision, a restricted administrative operation intended to isolate compromised portions of the Heroic Spirit system without immediately destroying its entire foundation. Under this application, Adam-Alaya may identify records, summoning channels, or spiritual connections that have been corrupted or appropriated by a hostile phenomenon and initiate a targeted intervention against their continued operation. A summoning pathway through which an enemy is acquiring unauthorized access to Heroic Spirit information may be severed, a compromised record may be isolated from further deployment, or a defensive summoning operation whose spiritual connection has become hostile to Human Order may be forcibly suspended. The purpose of Archive Excision is not necessarily to destroy the original Heroic Spirit record, but to prevent the compromised mechanism from continuing to function as an avenue through which humanity’s own accumulated legends can be turned against it. This distinction is particularly important when confronting enemies capable of copying Servant information, since preventing access through an authorized channel does not automatically eliminate every independent imitation already constructed through foreign means. An entity possessing a spiritual recording system that operates entirely outside Alaya’s administrative jurisdiction may remain capable of using that independent system even after the corresponding Human Order channel has been terminated. Nevertheless, Archive Excision provides an extraordinary safeguard against the corruption of the heroic defensive framework, allowing Adam-Alaya to restrict access to compromised resources before the threat escalates into a condition requiring the destruction of the entire repository. The second and true release of Thronus Ultimus is designated Termination of the Heroic Record, a catastrophic operation whose objective is the complete dismantlement of the Throne of Heroes as the system preserving and summoning recorded Heroic Spirits. Unlike Archive Excision, which attempts to preserve the wider system by removing compromised components, the full release rejects the continued existence of the system itself. Through the executive foundation of Alaya and the exceptional spiritual structure of the Grand Ruler, Adam-Alaya initiates a conceptual intervention against the higher-dimensional framework responsible for sustaining the recorded Heroic Spirits beyond the ordinary time axis. The operation does not function as an attack traveling through conventional space toward a geographically identifiable structure, for the Throne cannot be meaningfully treated as an ordinary physical object located somewhere within the material world. Instead, the Noble Phantasm targets the foundational relationship through which the Heroic Spirit records are maintained as enduring spiritual information and made available to summoning systems connected to Human Order. Upon successful completion, that relationship is terminated at its source, dismantling the mechanism responsible for preserving the recorded existences as Heroic Spirits. The resulting destruction is not limited to the Servants currently manifested in the world, nor does it merely prevent a single Holy Grail War from summoning additional participants. It eliminates the spiritual recording system upon which those manifestations depend, causing the Heroic Spirit records maintained by the affected Throne to cease existing in their preserved form. Kings, warriors, saints, magi, and other legendary individuals whose achievements had been recorded within the repository would no longer remain accessible as Heroic Spirits through the terminated system. The resulting loss would be catastrophic for Human Order, depriving humanity of one of its most extraordinary mechanisms for confronting future supernatural threats. However, the destruction of the Throne does not automatically rewrite the historical lives of those individuals, nor does it erase their achievements from the ordinary continuity of human civilization. A king who ruled in the past would still have ruled, a hero who accomplished extraordinary deeds would still have performed them, and the historical circumstances through which their legends emerged would not be retroactively invalidated merely because their preserved spiritual records had been destroyed. What is eliminated is the extraordinary condition through which their completed existences remain recorded and summonable beyond death. This distinction is essential because Thronus Ultimus is an Anti-Throne of Heroes Noble Phantasm rather than an Anti-History or Anti-Root phenomenon. Its power concerns the destruction of a particular higher-dimensional defensive framework, not unrestricted revision of causality or the elimination of every spiritual principle existing within Akasha. The conceptual consequences of the operation are nevertheless immense, as the Counter Force would lose access to a reservoir of heroic achievements accumulated throughout humanity’s historical and mythological existence. The full release therefore requires conditions far more restrictive than those governing an ordinary offensive Noble Phantasm. The Heroic Spirit system itself must have become an existential danger to humanity, Alaya must recognize that its continued operation presents a threat that cannot be adequately resolved through lesser measures, and Adam must consciously accept the decision to terminate the repository. The final requirement is particularly significant because Adam’s individuality remains the dominant consciousness within the composite Saint Graph. Alaya’s impersonal survival imperative may determine that sacrificing the Throne constitutes the only remaining means of preventing mankind’s extinction, but the execution of Thronus Ultimus is not permitted to bypass the personal judgment of the First Human. Adam understands that the Heroic Spirits preserved within the repository are not merely weapons or disposable records, but the accumulated legacies of individuals who possessed their own lives, ambitions, suffering, and achievements. The decision to terminate their preserved existences therefore represents an extraordinary moral burden, even if the operation is necessary to preserve the descendants whose survival gives the Counter Force its purpose. Furthermore, the full release of Thronus Ultimus is intrinsically self-destructive. Adam-Alaya’s unprecedented Grand Saint Graph is maintained through the direct convergence of Adam’s primordial spiritual foundation and Alaya’s collective existence, while its extraordinary administrative functions depend upon the wider relationship between Human Order and the spiritual infrastructure through which its guardians operate. By initiating the complete dismantlement of the heroic recording system, Adam-Alaya also destroys a fundamental portion of the structure supporting his own exceptional manifestation. The resulting instability causes the Grand Saint Graph to collapse upon completion of the Noble Phantasm, terminating the composite Servant’s existence as Adam-Alaya. This does not mean that the entire collective unconscious of humanity is annihilated, nor does it establish that the primordial identity of Adam is identical to the temporary Grand-class vessel created through their convergence. Rather, the particular spiritual existence known as Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya loses the conditions necessary to continue manifesting and cannot simply return through the heroic system he has destroyed. The sacrifice is therefore inseparable from the full operation, making Thronus Ultimus a genuinely final Noble Phantasm rather than a destructive technique that can be activated repeatedly without consequence. Its relationship with Thronus Resonans further emphasizes the paradox, for the fifth Noble Phantasm depends upon the preservation and accessibility of complete Heroic Spirit records, while Thronus Ultimus possesses the capacity to eliminate the very repository from which those records are obtained. Once the full termination has been completed, the ordinary mechanisms through which Thronus Resonans functions can no longer operate, and the accumulated heroic power that once served humanity’s defense becomes permanently inaccessible through the destroyed system. Thronus Ultimus is thus an ability whose significance cannot be adequately measured through conventional offensive parameters, as it does not demonstrate supremacy through the amount of physical territory it can devastate or the number of enemies it can defeat in direct combat. Its destructive scope is administrative, conceptual, and systemic, targeting an irreplaceable foundation of Human Order rather than an ordinary opponent. The EX rank consequently represents the exceptional nature of an operation capable of dismantling the higher-dimensional repository of humanity’s Heroic Spirits, while its activation restrictions reflect the catastrophic consequences such an intervention would impose upon mankind’s future. In philosophical terms, Thronus Ultimus represents the ultimate contradiction of the First Father’s responsibility. Adam-Alaya possesses the ability to call upon the achievements of his descendants to preserve humanity, yet he also possesses the terrible authority to bring an end to their continued service if the preservation of their records becomes incompatible with mankind’s survival. The Noble Phantasm does not express contempt for heroes or a desire to eliminate the legends humanity has accumulated. It represents the possibility that the guardian of mankind may someday be forced to destroy one of humanity’s greatest defensive achievements in order to preserve the lives for whose sake those achievements were recorded. Thronus Ultimus is therefore not simply the destruction of the Throne of Heroes, but the final acknowledgment that even the most sacred instruments of Human Order must remain subordinate to the continued existence of the humanity they were created to protect.

V. Thronus Resonans: The Throne Shall Answer Humanity’s Final Call — Rank: EX. Classification: Anti-Ineffectuality. Range: 1–1000 Maximum Targets: 1000. is the fifth Noble Phantasm possessed by Grand Ruler Adam-Alaya and the greatest offensive manifestation of his administrative relationship with the Throne of Heroes, representing the conversion of humanity’s accumulated heroic records into immediate acts of defensive intervention through the deliberate violation of the limitations ordinarily imposed upon Servant containers. Whereas conventional Heroic Spirit summoning reproduces a restricted manifestation of an individual’s recorded existence within an appropriate class vessel, allowing a portion of the Heroic Spirit’s abilities, parameters, and Noble Phantasms to operate as a comparatively stable spiritual entity, Thronus Resonans rejects the necessity of maintaining such stability and instead prioritizes the complete manifestation of the Heroic Record for the duration required to unleash its greatest available power. The Noble Phantasm originates from the extraordinary administrative privileges conferred by Adam-Alaya’s direct convergence with Alaya, permitting the Grand Ruler to access the records of Heroic Spirits through Human Order and project their completed spiritual information into specially constructed temporary Servant containers. These manifestations are designated Spectral Servants, although the term must not be confused with conventional Shadow Servants or weakened spiritual copies, for the defining characteristic of a Spectral Servant is not the incompleteness of its recorded abilities, but the impossibility of sustaining their completeness within the container provided. A conventional Servant ordinarily represents a selected manifestation of a Heroic Spirit, with the class system establishing the limits through which that Heroic Spirit may appear in the world. Thronus Resonans reverses the relationship between record and vessel. Rather than reducing the manifested information until it becomes compatible with a stable Saint Graph, Adam-Alaya constructs an ephemeral container and forces the complete compatible Heroic Record into it, preserving the powers, experiences, abilities, and Noble Phantasms recorded within that spiritual existence without imposing the ordinary reductions necessary for prolonged manifestation. The resulting Spectral Servant therefore possesses the full capabilities represented by the completed record, reproducing the heroic existence at the height of its recorded power, including the extraordinary abilities it possessed during its living prime and the supernatural significance accumulated through its legend. This does not mean that contradictory incarnations, mutually exclusive possibilities, or entirely separate spiritual identities are indiscriminately combined into one impossible manifestation, but that the selected compatible record is manifested without the ordinary loss of information associated with a restricted class container. The consequence is immediate structural instability. The quantity and complexity of spiritual information contained within the Spectral Servant exceed the capacity of its temporary Saint Graph, causing the vessel to begin deteriorating from the moment of manifestation. Its spiritual pathways become overloaded, the stability of its external body progressively collapses, and the continued existence of the manifestation becomes impossible under ordinary conditions. Adam-Alaya does not attempt to eliminate this instability, because the Noble Phantasm is deliberately constructed around the interval between manifestation and collapse. Rather than creating a conventional Servant capable of sustained combat, Thronus Resonans produces a temporary Heroic Spirit manifestation designed to perform a single decisive action before its vessel fails. Upon construction of the Spectral Saint Graph, the strongest applicable Noble Phantasm possessed by the corresponding Heroic Record is prepared for immediate release, with the necessary magical energy supplied through Alaya’s available defensive resources and the target designated through Adam-Alaya’s executive authority. The Spectral Servant therefore appears upon the battlefield with its ultimate attack already approaching activation, requiring neither a prolonged period of combat nor the ordinary distribution of magical energy across an extended manifestation. Once the target has been established, the Spectral Servant immediately invokes its Noble Phantasm, releasing the greatest output permitted by its complete record and the resources supplied for the intervention. Following the discharge, the already-overloaded Saint Graph reaches the limit of its structural tolerance and collapses, causing the temporary body to disintegrate and its projected spiritual information to return to the Throne of Heroes. The destruction of the temporary vessel does not eliminate the original Heroic Spirit record, for the process involves the manifestation of recorded information rather than the permanent extraction and consumption of the original spiritual existence. As a result, the same Heroic Record may remain available for future authorized interventions, provided that the Throne itself remains intact and sufficient resources can be supplied for another manifestation. The conceptual principle underlying this process is designated Anti-Ineffectuality, an exceptional classification that does not represent the direct negation of an opponent’s defenses, the cancellation of all resistance, or an automatic guarantee that a released Noble Phantasm will defeat its target. Rather, it concerns the elimination of the limitations that ordinarily prevent a Heroic Spirit’s complete recorded power from being realized within a Servant container. A conventional summoning system must preserve the functionality of the vessel, and therefore restricts the manifested record to a form that can remain stable for the intended duration. Thronus Resonans rejects the requirement of prolonged stability altogether, treating the container’s inevitable destruction as an acceptable cost of obtaining immediate access to the complete heroic power recorded within it. The limitation of the vessel is not overcome by making it infinitely durable, but rendered irrelevant to the immediate objective of releasing the Noble Phantasm. Thus, a Spectral Servant may possess extraordinary combat abilities that would normally require a far more capable spiritual container, yet the manifestation needs to survive only long enough for those abilities to be expressed through a single decisive discharge. The operational significance of this principle becomes especially apparent when considering Heroic Spirits whose greatest Noble Phantasms possess severe costs, exceptional activation conditions, or consequences incompatible with prolonged combat. In cases where the necessary requirements can be supplied or incorporated into the Spectral manifestation, the inability of the container to survive afterward ceases to be a meaningful disadvantage, since the vessel was never intended to continue existing beyond the attack. Nevertheless, Thronus Resonans does not automatically ignore every inherent condition attached to a Noble Phantasm, nor does it provide an unlimited means of reproducing mysteries whose foundations are fundamentally inaccessible to the selected record. A Noble Phantasm requiring a particular Authority, spiritual state, or conceptual prerequisite must still possess a viable method of satisfying that requirement within the manifestation process. The greatest operational advantage of Thronus Resonans lies in its Complete Heroic Record Mobilization, through which Adam-Alaya may select not merely one suitable Heroic Spirit, but multiple records whose powers collectively provide the greatest available response to a designated threat. Because his individual consciousness is integrated with Alaya’s collective awareness, Adam-Alaya can evaluate the abilities of accessible Heroic Spirits according to the nature of the opponent, selecting records whose Noble Phantasms possess appropriate conceptual properties, destructive capabilities, or interactions with the enemy’s known vulnerabilities. These selections may include ordinary Heroic Spirits associated with the conventional seven classes, exceptionally powerful heroes whose records contain Divine Constructs or extraordinary supernatural mysteries, and individuals possessing qualifications for Grand-class manifestation. In the latter case, Thronus Resonans is capable of establishing Spectral Grand Servants, exceptional temporary manifestations whose containers reproduce the appropriate Grand-class foundation while simultaneously incorporating the completed record of the qualified heroic existence. Such manifestations are not merely ordinary Servants granted a decorative Grand designation, for the corresponding spiritual foundation must actually be supplied through the authorization and resources of the Counter Force. When the required conditions are satisfied, however, the resulting Spectral Grand Servant can unleash the extraordinary power associated with its Grand-class manifestation and completed Heroic Record, even though the temporary container remains incapable of sustaining that information beyond the immediate release. The extraordinary resource expenditure required to construct such a vessel means that Grand-class manifestations are considerably more demanding than conventional Spectral Servants, but the Noble Phantasm possesses no inherent restriction requiring Adam-Alaya to summon only a single Grand-class record at a time. Through the simultaneous construction of multiple Spectral Saint Graphs, Adam-Alaya can coordinate the manifestation of several Heroic Spirits within the same operation, allowing each to release its strongest applicable Noble Phantasm against a designated target or set of targets. The number of simultaneous manifestations is determined by the available Counter Force resources, the complexity of the selected records, and the capacity of the Grand Ruler’s spiritual foundation to coordinate their release, rather than by an arbitrary requirement corresponding to the seven conventional Servant classes. Under exceptional authorization, an immense formation of Spectral Servants may therefore appear upon the battlefield, each carrying the complete record of a different heroic existence and each prepared to release its ultimate attack before the collapse of its temporary vessel. The resulting phenomenon is not simply an army of Servants, for such an army would ordinarily require the maintenance of individual spiritual bodies, the distribution of magical energy across prolonged combat, and the coordination of numerous independent engagements. Thronus Resonans instead converts those spiritual manifestations into a synchronized sequence of decisive Noble Phantasm releases, concentrating the accumulated heroic achievements of mankind into an exceptionally brief interval. The battlefield may become filled with the appearances of legendary kings, warriors, magi, saints, and other extraordinary individuals, their spiritual bodies already exhibiting fractures caused by the intolerable density of their completed records. Before the enemy can engage them through ordinary combat, their Noble Phantasms are activated, producing a convergence of legendary weapons, conceptual phenomena, and high-order supernatural mysteries whose combined operation has been selected according to the nature of the threat. This does not imply that every Noble Phantasm can be released simultaneously without interference, as incompatible effects may require sequential activation or separation into different formations. Through Primordial Covenant and Collective Experience of Mankind, Adam-Alaya can coordinate the timing and selection of the manifestations, attempting to prevent conflicting abilities from diminishing the overall effectiveness of the intervention. Should the enemy survive the initial discharge, the results become information for the Counter Force’s continued threat assessment, permitting Adam-Alaya to select different records, modify the order of deployment, or concentrate resources upon a more appropriate conceptual countermeasure. As long as Alaya remains capable of supplying the necessary energy and the Throne of Heroes remains accessible, successive formations may be established, each drawing upon the heroic records available to Human Order. Theoretically, the number and quality of such formations could become extraordinary during a genuine extinction-level crisis, when the collective survival imperative of mankind justifies the expenditure of resources far beyond those allocated during an ordinary Servant conflict. Nevertheless, the system is not without vulnerabilities. The complete Heroic Records must actually be accessible through the relevant spiritual framework, and an existence that has never been recorded within the applicable Throne cannot be manifested merely because Adam-Alaya is aware of its legend. The construction of a temporary vessel also requires genuine magical energy, and the manifestation of numerous exceptional or Grand-class records can impose a tremendous burden upon the resources available to the Counter Force. Furthermore, an enemy capable of interfering with the Heroic Spirit system, absorbing spiritual information, or establishing independent control over a compromised summoning channel may threaten the integrity of the deployment process. Adam-Alaya’s administrative functions provide extraordinary safeguards against such interference, particularly through the restricted Archive Excision function of Thronus Ultimus, but they cannot guarantee perfect resistance against every superior or foreign phenomenon. The destruction of a Spectral Servant’s temporary container also prevents the summoned manifestation from engaging in prolonged independent combat, meaning that a Noble Phantasm that fails to achieve its intended effect cannot necessarily be followed by ordinary tactical adjustments from the same manifested Servant. Instead, a new formation or another projection must be employed, provided that sufficient resources remain available. These limitations distinguish Thronus Resonans from unrestricted summoning omnipotence, while preserving the extraordinary significance of its Anti-Ineffectuality classification. Its fundamental achievement is the ability to bring the completed power of recorded Heroic Spirits into the world without requiring their containers to remain stable after the immediate execution of their greatest Noble Phantasms. Yet the deepest significance of Thronus Resonans lies in its relationship with Adam himself. As the primordial human, Adam represents the beginning of the lineage whose accumulated achievements are preserved within the Throne of Heroes. Alaya represents the collective survival instinct through which those achievements may be called upon to defend humanity. Their convergence therefore creates an unprecedented relationship between the origin of mankind and the records of those who followed him, allowing the First Human to call upon the complete heroic legacies of his descendants when the continuation of humanity is threatened. Adam does not regard these manifestations as disposable possessions, despite the fact that their temporary containers are deliberately constructed to collapse. He recognizes that each record represents an individual existence whose accomplishments, suffering, and choices contributed to the history of mankind, and that the power he employs is not fundamentally his own achievement. His role is to establish the conditions through which their accumulated legends may answer the collective desire for another tomorrow. This distinction also explains why the Noble Phantasm’s greatest manifestation is not necessarily accompanied by triumph or exultation. To Adam, the appearance of countless Spectral Servants represents humanity once again calling upon those who have already completed their lives to preserve the future of those who remain. Their immediate disappearance following the release of their Noble Phantasms is not treated as an insignificant mechanical consequence, but as the conclusion of a final act of service performed through the records of their heroic existences. Thronus Resonans thus embodies the paradoxical relationship between the First Father and the Throne of Heroes: the man from whom humanity began possesses the ability to call upon the greatest achievements of his descendants, yet those achievements remain the legacies of individuals who lived long after him and whose accomplishments belong to themselves. Its EX rank reflects the unprecedented nature of a summoning operation capable of manifesting complete Heroic Records, potentially including authorized Grand-class foundations, for the duration necessary to unleash their greatest Noble Phantasms. Thronus Resonans is therefore the Noble Phantasm through which humanity’s accumulated heroic history becomes an immediate defensive response, permitting the First Human to call upon the completed records of those who came after him so that those who have not yet been born may inherit another tomorrow.
